window.PORTAL_DATA = {"overview":{"problem":"Cooperative GIG helps labour cooperatives connect skilled workers with household and community service requests while making workforce coordination, fair work allocation and accountability easier.","mvp":"The web-first MVP supports individual customers from service discovery through request, fair allocation, assignment, completion and payment-status recording. Institutional customers are outside MVP.","sourceFiles":["project-scope.md","SRS.md","feature-inventory.md","proposed-mvp.md"]},"requirements":[{"id":"FR-AUTH-001","text":"The platform shall authenticate users before allowing access to protected functionality.","section":"Accounts and access management"},{"id":"FR-AUTH-002","text":"The platform shall support role-based permissions.","section":"Accounts and access management"},{"id":"FR-AUTH-003","text":"Authorization shall account for organizational scope, including the user's permitted state or cooperative.","section":"Accounts and access management"},{"id":"FR-AUTH-004","text":"Users shall be able to maintain permitted account and profile information.","section":"Accounts and access management"},{"id":"FR-AUTH-005","text":"The platform shall support appropriate account verification, recovery and status-management processes.","section":"Accounts and access management"},{"id":"FR-AUTH-006","text":"Unauthorized access to protected records or operations shall be rejected.","section":"Accounts and access management"},{"id":"FR-AUTH-007","text":"The platform shall distinguish user identity, role, organizational affiliation and assigned permissions.","section":"Accounts and access management"},{"id":"FR-SVC-001","text":"Customers shall be able to browse available service categories and descriptions.","section":"Service catalogue and discovery"},{"id":"FR-SVC-002","text":"Customers shall be able to identify cooperatives offering relevant services.","section":"Service catalogue and discovery"},{"id":"FR-SVC-003","text":"The platform shall maintain information about service requirements and applicable service conditions.","section":"Service catalogue and discovery"},{"id":"FR-SVC-004","text":"Authorized cooperative personnel shall be able to maintain their service listings.","section":"Service catalogue and discovery"},{"id":"FR-SVC-005","text":"The platform shall support relevant discovery criteria, such as location and service category, where applicable.","section":"Service catalogue and discovery"},{"id":"FR-SVC-006","text":"Pricing information shall distinguish fixed prices, indicative prices and prices requiring negotiation.","section":"Service catalogue and discovery"},{"id":"FR-REQ-001","text":"Customers shall be able to submit service requests with the required service details.","section":"Customer service requests"},{"id":"FR-REQ-002","text":"Requests shall record relevant information, including location, preferred schedule and work description.","section":"Customer service requests"},{"id":"FR-REQ-003","text":"Customers may provide an optional budget or expected price range.","section":"Customer service requests"},{"id":"FR-REQ-004","text":"The platform shall validate required request information before accepting submission.","section":"Customer service requests"},{"id":"FR-REQ-005","text":"Each submitted request shall receive a unique identifier.","section":"Customer service requests"},{"id":"FR-REQ-006","text":"The platform shall make requests available to the appropriate cooperative for review.","section":"Customer service requests"},{"id":"FR-REQ-007","text":"Authorized managers shall be able to accept a request for processing, reject it or request clarification.","section":"Customer service requests"},{"id":"FR-REQ-008","text":"Customers shall be able to view the status of their requests.","section":"Customer service requests"},{"id":"FR-REQ-009","text":"The platform shall support permitted cancellation and rescheduling requests.","section":"Customer service requests"},{"id":"FR-REQ-010","text":"Customers shall be able to view relevant historical requests and outcomes.","section":"Customer service requests"},{"id":"FR-WRK-001","text":"The platform shall maintain worker profiles containing relevant skills and service-related information.","section":"Worker profiles and lifecycle"},{"id":"FR-WRK-002","text":"Workers shall be associated with the appropriate cooperative or cooperatives according to the approved membership model.","section":"Worker profiles and lifecycle"},{"id":"FR-WRK-003","text":"Authorized personnel shall be able to verify worker information and manage eligibility status.","section":"Worker profiles and lifecycle"},{"id":"FR-WRK-004","text":"The platform shall record worker availability information where provided.","section":"Worker profiles and lifecycle"},{"id":"FR-WRK-005","text":"Workers shall be able to view their assignment offers and confirmed assignments.","section":"Worker profiles and lifecycle"},{"id":"FR-WRK-006","text":"Workers shall be able to accept or reject assignment offers.","section":"Worker profiles and lifecycle"},{"id":"FR-WRK-007","text":"The platform shall record the response and timestamp for each assignment offer.","section":"Worker profiles and lifecycle"},{"id":"FR-WRK-008","text":"Workers shall be able to update job progress through permitted status transitions.","section":"Worker profiles and lifecycle"},{"id":"FR-WRK-009","text":"Workers shall be able to report unavailability, delays or inability to complete a job.","section":"Worker profiles and lifecycle"},{"id":"FR-WRK-010","text":"The platform shall retain relevant worker assignment and completion history.","section":"Worker profiles and lifecycle"},{"id":"FR-WRK-011","text":"Workers or authorized personnel shall be able to maintain recorded worker availability according to the approved availability policy.","section":"Worker profiles and lifecycle"},{"id":"FR-RANK-001","text":"The platform shall implement an algorithm to rank workers for a service request.","section":"Worker-ranking algorithm"},{"id":"FR-RANK-002","text":"The algorithm shall evaluate workers against the request's relevant skill, service and other suitability requirements.","section":"Worker-ranking algorithm"},{"id":"FR-RANK-003","text":"The algorithm shall consider workload and previous job allocations to support equitable distribution of opportunities.","section":"Worker-ranking algorithm"},{"id":"FR-RANK-004","text":"The algorithm shall consider recorded availability as a relevant factor according to the approved ranking policy, but unavailable status shall not automatically prevent an assignment offer from being sent.","section":"Worker-ranking algorithm"},{"id":"FR-RANK-005","text":"The platform shall present ranked recommendations to an authorized cooperative manager.","section":"Worker-ranking algorithm"},{"id":"FR-RANK-006","text":"The platform shall allow an authorized manager to select a candidate from the recommended workers, subject to eligibility and governance rules.","section":"Worker-ranking algorithm"},{"id":"FR-RANK-007","text":"The platform shall record the selected worker and relevant assignment decision information.","section":"Worker-ranking algorithm"},{"id":"FR-RANK-008","text":"The platform shall retain sufficient allocation history to evaluate the distribution of opportunities.","section":"Worker-ranking algorithm"},{"id":"FR-RANK-009","text":"The platform shall support monitoring for persistent imbalances in job opportunities.","section":"Worker-ranking algorithm"},{"id":"FR-RANK-010","text":"The platform shall support the recording of justified manager overrides according to the approved policy.","section":"Worker-ranking algorithm"},{"id":"FR-ASG-001","text":"An authorized cooperative manager shall be able to send an assignment offer to a selected worker.","section":"Assignment offers and acceptance"},{"id":"FR-ASG-002","text":"An offer may be sent even if the worker's recorded availability indicates that they are unavailable.","section":"Assignment offers and acceptance"},{"id":"FR-ASG-003","text":"The worker shall be able to accept or reject the offer.","section":"Assignment offers and acceptance"},{"id":"FR-ASG-004","text":"The platform shall record the offer's pending, accepted, rejected or expired state as applicable.","section":"Assignment offers and acceptance"},{"id":"FR-ASG-005","text":"A rejected or expired offer shall not become a confirmed assignment.","section":"Assignment offers and acceptance"},{"id":"FR-ASG-006","text":"The platform shall support offering the job to another ranked candidate after rejection or expiry.","section":"Assignment offers and acceptance"},{"id":"FR-ASG-007","text":"The platform shall prevent incompatible confirmed assignments according to the approved scheduling rules.","section":"Assignment offers and acceptance"},{"id":"FR-ASG-008","text":"An accepted offer shall proceed to the required price and scope agreement process when negotiation is necessary.","section":"Assignment offers and acceptance"},{"id":"FR-ASG-009","text":"A confirmed assignment shall satisfy the applicable worker-acceptance, customer-agreement and cooperative-approval conditions.","section":"Assignment offers and acceptance"},{"id":"FR-ASG-010","text":"The platform shall retain a traceable history of offers, responses and assignment changes.","section":"Assignment offers and acceptance"},{"id":"FR-NEG-001","text":"The platform shall support negotiated pricing for services without a predefined fixed price.","section":"Price negotiation"},{"id":"FR-NEG-002","text":"Workers shall be able to submit a quote for the proposed service.","section":"Price negotiation"},{"id":"FR-NEG-003","text":"A quote may include the proposed amount, work scope, estimated duration, cost breakdown and payment terms where applicable.","section":"Price negotiation"},{"id":"FR-NEG-004","text":"Customers shall be able to accept a quote, reject it, request clarification or submit a counteroffer.","section":"Price negotiation"},{"id":"FR-NEG-005","text":"Workers shall be able to respond to counteroffers.","section":"Price negotiation"},{"id":"FR-NEG-006","text":"The platform shall maintain a history of quotes, counteroffers and revisions.","section":"Price negotiation"},{"id":"FR-NEG-007","text":"The platform shall distinguish proposed prices from the final agreed price.","section":"Price negotiation"},{"id":"FR-NEG-008","text":"The platform shall record the final agreed amount, work scope, schedule and payment terms.","section":"Price negotiation"},{"id":"FR-NEG-009","text":"The platform shall not treat the price as agreed until the required parties have accepted the same terms.","section":"Price negotiation"},{"id":"FR-NEG-010","text":"The platform shall support negotiation expiry or timeout policies if adopted.","section":"Price negotiation"},{"id":"FR-NEG-011","text":"If the parties cannot agree, the request shall follow the approved decline, closure or reassignment process.","section":"Price negotiation"},{"id":"FR-NEG-012","text":"Changes to agreed work scope or price shall require the applicable approvals and a recorded revision.","section":"Price negotiation"},{"id":"FR-PAY-001","text":"The platform shall maintain the agreed price and payment terms associated with a service.","section":"Payment management"},{"id":"FR-PAY-002","text":"The platform shall support a configurable payment model appropriate to the service and cooperative policy.","section":"Payment management"},{"id":"FR-PAY-003","text":"The platform shall record payment obligations and outstanding balances.","section":"Payment management"},{"id":"FR-PAY-004","text":"The platform shall record payment status and relevant transaction information.","section":"Payment management"},{"id":"FR-PAY-005","text":"The platform shall distinguish a declared cash payment from a digitally verified transaction.","section":"Payment management"},{"id":"FR-PAY-006","text":"Digital payment integration may be supported through an approved payment provider.","section":"Payment management"},{"id":"FR-PAY-007","text":"The platform shall support recording of refunds, adjustments or partial payments where applicable.","section":"Payment management"},{"id":"FR-PAY-008","text":"The platform shall support authorized review of payment disputes.","section":"Payment management"},{"id":"FR-PAY-009","text":"The platform shall maintain a traceable history of financial status changes.","section":"Payment management"},{"id":"FR-PAY-010","text":"Financial information shall be accessible only to authorized users.","section":"Payment management"},{"id":"FR-PAY-011","text":"Cooperative fees, commissions or revenue-sharing rules shall be configurable according to an approved policy rather than assuming one universal fee.","section":"Payment management"},{"id":"FR-PAY-012","text":"The platform shall distinguish recording a payment from independently confirming that the money has been received.","section":"Payment management"},{"id":"FR-JOB-001","text":"Workers shall be able to view the details of their confirmed jobs.","section":"Job execution and completion"},{"id":"FR-JOB-002","text":"Workers shall be able to update job status through permitted transitions.","section":"Job execution and completion"},{"id":"FR-JOB-003","text":"The platform shall record relevant progress and timestamps.","section":"Job execution and completion"},{"id":"FR-JOB-004","text":"Workers shall be able to report delays or inability to complete a job.","section":"Job execution and completion"},{"id":"FR-JOB-005","text":"The platform shall support completion information or evidence where required.","section":"Job execution and completion"},{"id":"FR-JOB-006","text":"The platform shall support the approved completion-verification process.","section":"Job execution and completion"},{"id":"FR-JOB-007","text":"Customers shall be able to view permitted job progress and completion information.","section":"Job execution and completion"},{"id":"FR-JOB-008","text":"The platform shall retain final job records and relevant assignment history.","section":"Job execution and completion"},{"id":"FR-JOB-009","text":"The platform shall support cancellation, reassignment and exception handling.","section":"Job execution and completion"},{"id":"FR-JOB-010","text":"The platform shall support customer feedback and service-related complaints where enabled.","section":"Job execution and completion"},{"id":"FR-JOB-011","text":"Customers and institutional customers shall be able to view permitted assignment information after an assignment is confirmed, subject to role and organizational access rules.","section":"Job execution and completion"},{"id":"FR-COOP-001","text":"Authorized managers shall be able to maintain cooperative profiles and service listings.","section":"Cooperative management"},{"id":"FR-COOP-002","text":"Managers shall be able to manage worker records within their authorized scope.","section":"Cooperative management"},{"id":"FR-COOP-003","text":"Managers shall be able to review and process incoming service requests.","section":"Cooperative management"},{"id":"FR-COOP-004","text":"Managers shall be able to view ranked worker recommendations.","section":"Cooperative management"},{"id":"FR-COOP-005","text":"Managers shall be able to send assignment offers and monitor responses.","section":"Cooperative management"},{"id":"FR-COOP-006","text":"Managers shall be able to monitor active jobs and completion status.","section":"Cooperative management"},{"id":"FR-COOP-007","text":"Managers shall be able to handle operational exceptions and reassignment.","section":"Cooperative management"},{"id":"FR-COOP-008","text":"Managers shall be able to review relevant customer feedback and complaints.","section":"Cooperative management"},{"id":"FR-COOP-009","text":"Managers shall be able to access relevant workforce and service-delivery reports.","section":"Cooperative management"},{"id":"FR-COOP-010","text":"Cooperative records shall be protected from unauthorized access by other cooperatives.","section":"Cooperative management"},{"id":"FR-ADM-001","text":"The platform shall support authorized platform-wide monitoring.","section":"Central and state administration"},{"id":"FR-ADM-002","text":"Central administrators shall be able to view permitted aggregated platform indicators and reports.","section":"Central and state administration"},{"id":"FR-ADM-003","text":"State administrators shall be able to register cooperatives within their authorized state scope.","section":"Central and state administration"},{"id":"FR-ADM-004","text":"State administrators shall be able to maintain authorized cooperative records.","section":"Central and state administration"},{"id":"FR-ADM-005","text":"State administrators shall be able to view relevant state-scoped operational reports.","section":"Central and state administration"},{"id":"FR-ADM-006","text":"Administrative permissions shall be explicitly defined and enforced.","section":"Central and state administration"},{"id":"FR-ADM-007","text":"Important administrative actions shall be recorded.","section":"Central and state administration"},{"id":"FR-ADM-008","text":"Central monitoring shall not automatically grant unrestricted access to every cooperative's operational data.","section":"Central and state administration"},{"id":"FR-ADM-009","text":"Cooperatives operating at a central level shall retain cooperative-management functionality.","section":"Central and state administration"},{"id":"FR-ADM-010","text":"The platform shall support escalation of issues between the appropriate administrative levels.","section":"Central and state administration"},{"id":"FR-ADM-011","text":"Changes to shared policies and allocation rules shall require authorized control and shall be traceable to the responsible actor, effective time and policy version.","section":"Central and state administration"},{"id":"FR-INS-001","text":"Authorized institutional representatives shall be able to submit service requirements.","section":"Institutional service management"},{"id":"FR-INS-002","text":"Institutional requests shall record relevant scope, location, schedule and workforce needs.","section":"Institutional service management"},{"id":"FR-INS-003","text":"Cooperatives shall be able to review institutional requests and assess feasibility.","section":"Institutional service management"},{"id":"FR-INS-004","text":"The platform shall record acceptance, rejection or requests for clarification.","section":"Institutional service management"},{"id":"FR-INS-005","text":"Accepted institutional requests shall support workforce coordination and job tracking.","section":"Institutional service management"},{"id":"FR-INS-006","text":"Institutions shall be able to view permitted service-delivery records.","section":"Institutional service management"},{"id":"FR-INS-007","text":"Institutions shall be able to submit feedback or complaints.","section":"Institutional service management"},{"id":"FR-INS-008","text":"The platform may support formal contracts, tenders and procurement workflows if validated.","section":"Institutional service management"},{"id":"FR-INS-009","text":"Authorized institutional representatives shall be able to maintain permitted institutional organization and contact information.","section":"Institutional service management"},{"id":"FR-INS-010","text":"Authorized institutional representatives shall be able to access relevant service-delivery reports within their permitted scope.","section":"Institutional service management"},{"id":"FR-INS-011","text":"Institutional users may access permitted financial records when the corresponding payment and financial-reporting capabilities are implemented.","section":"Institutional service management"},{"id":"FR-NOT-001","text":"The platform shall notify relevant parties of request and booking status changes.","section":"Notifications and communication"},{"id":"FR-NOT-002","text":"Workers shall receive assignment-offer notifications.","section":"Notifications and communication"},{"id":"FR-NOT-003","text":"Customers and workers shall receive relevant quote and counteroffer updates.","section":"Notifications and communication"},{"id":"FR-NOT-004","text":"The platform shall communicate accepted, rejected or expired assignment offers.","section":"Notifications and communication"},{"id":"FR-NOT-005","text":"The platform shall communicate relevant cancellation, completion and payment-status changes.","section":"Notifications and communication"},{"id":"FR-NOT-006","text":"Notification delivery status shall be tracked where supported by the delivery channel.","section":"Notifications and communication"},{"id":"FR-DSP-001","text":"Customers shall be able to report service-related issues.","section":"Feedback, complaints and disputes"},{"id":"FR-DSP-002","text":"The platform shall record complaint status and relevant history.","section":"Feedback, complaints and disputes"},{"id":"FR-DSP-003","text":"Authorized personnel shall be able to review and resolve complaints.","section":"Feedback, complaints and disputes"},{"id":"FR-DSP-004","text":"The platform shall support escalation of unresolved issues.","section":"Feedback, complaints and disputes"},{"id":"FR-DSP-005","text":"Disputes relating to work scope, completion, price or payment shall be recorded separately from ordinary booking status.","section":"Feedback, complaints and disputes"},{"id":"FR-DSP-006","text":"Resolution decisions shall be attributable to authorized personnel.","section":"Feedback, complaints and disputes"},{"id":"FR-REP-001","text":"Cooperatives shall be able to review relevant service-request and completion information.","section":"Reporting and analytics"},{"id":"FR-REP-002","text":"Authorized personnel shall be able to review worker workload and utilization.","section":"Reporting and analytics"},{"id":"FR-REP-003","text":"The platform shall support analysis of job-allocation patterns.","section":"Reporting and analytics"},{"id":"FR-REP-004","text":"State administrators shall be able to access permitted state-level reports.","section":"Reporting and analytics"},{"id":"FR-REP-005","text":"Central administrators shall be able to access permitted platform-level reports.","section":"Reporting and analytics"},{"id":"FR-REP-006","text":"Financial reporting may be supported if payment and settlement capabilities are adopted.","section":"Reporting and analytics"},{"id":"FR-REP-007","text":"Reports shall respect role and organizational access boundaries.","section":"Reporting and analytics"},{"id":"BR-001","text":"Every request must have a unique identifier.","section":"Request and assignment rules"},{"id":"BR-002","text":"Submission does not mean the request has been accepted.","section":"Request and assignment rules"},{"id":"BR-003","text":"Only an authorized manager can initiate an assignment offer on behalf of a cooperative.","section":"Request and assignment rules"},{"id":"BR-004","text":"An assignment offer is not a confirmed assignment.","section":"Request and assignment rules"},{"id":"BR-005","text":"A worker must respond to an assignment offer by accepting or rejecting it.","section":"Request and assignment rules"},{"id":"BR-006","text":"Rejected or expired offers must not become confirmed assignments.","section":"Request and assignment rules"},{"id":"BR-007","text":"The platform must prevent incompatible confirmed assignments under the approved scheduling rules.","section":"Request and assignment rules"},{"id":"BR-008","text":"Confirmed assignments must satisfy the applicable acceptance and service-agreement requirements.","section":"Request and assignment rules"},{"id":"BR-009","text":"Worker recommendations must follow documented ranking rules.","section":"Fair allocation rules"},{"id":"BR-010","text":"Suitability requirements must be considered alongside fair opportunity.","section":"Fair allocation rules"},{"id":"BR-011","text":"Availability information must not automatically block an offer under the currently intended workflow.","section":"Fair allocation rules"},{"id":"BR-012","text":"Allocation history must be retained sufficiently to evaluate opportunity distribution.","section":"Fair allocation rules"},{"id":"BR-013","text":"Manager overrides must follow the approved policy.","section":"Fair allocation rules"},{"id":"BR-014","text":"Fairness must be evaluated using defined indicators rather than assuming that equal job counts always constitute fairness.","section":"Fair allocation rules"},{"id":"BR-029","text":"Fair-allocation rules must not bypass mandatory suitability, safety or service-eligibility requirements merely to equalize opportunity measures.","section":"Fair allocation rules"},{"id":"BR-015","text":"A proposed quote is not a final agreed price.","section":"Negotiation and financial rules"},{"id":"BR-016","text":"The required parties must agree to the same terms before the service is confirmed under the negotiated-pricing workflow.","section":"Negotiation and financial rules"},{"id":"BR-017","text":"Changes to agreed scope or price require the applicable approvals.","section":"Negotiation and financial rules"},{"id":"BR-018","text":"Payment records must distinguish amounts due, payments declared, transactions confirmed and balances outstanding.","section":"Negotiation and financial rules"},{"id":"BR-019","text":"A recorded cash payment must not be represented as independently verified unless the platform has an appropriate verification basis.","section":"Negotiation and financial rules"},{"id":"BR-020","text":"Fees and revenue sharing must follow an approved cooperative or platform policy.","section":"Negotiation and financial rules"},{"id":"BR-021","text":"Payment disputes must follow the approved review and resolution process.","section":"Negotiation and financial rules"},{"id":"BR-022","text":"Users may access only the functions and records authorized for their role and organizational scope.","section":"Governance and data rules"},{"id":"BR-023","text":"State administrators must operate within their authorized state scope.","section":"Governance and data rules"},{"id":"BR-024","text":"Cooperative managers must be restricted to their authorized cooperative records.","section":"Governance and data rules"},{"id":"BR-025","text":"Central monitoring privileges must not automatically imply unrestricted operational authority.","section":"Governance and data rules"},{"id":"BR-026","text":"Significant request, assignment, negotiation, financial and administrative changes must be traceable.","section":"Governance and data rules"},{"id":"BR-027","text":"Job statuses must follow permitted transitions.","section":"Governance and data rules"},{"id":"BR-028","text":"Data access and reporting must respect applicable privacy requirements.","section":"Governance and data rules"},{"id":"NFR-SEC-001","text":"Protected functionality must require authentication.","section":"Security"},{"id":"NFR-SEC-002","text":"Authorization must be enforced by backend services.","section":"Security"},{"id":"NFR-SEC-003","text":"Sensitive information must be protected against unauthorized access.","section":"Security"},{"id":"NFR-SEC-004","text":"Passwords, tokens, credentials and application secrets must be handled securely.","section":"Security"},{"id":"NFR-SEC-005","text":"Inputs must be validated, and errors must not expose secrets or sensitive implementation details.","section":"Security"},{"id":"NFR-SEC-006","text":"Security testing must cover critical workflows and access boundaries.","section":"Security"},{"id":"NFR-SEC-007","text":"The platform shall support approved policies and controlled processes for data retention, correction and deletion, subject to legal, audit and dispute-preservation requirements.","section":"Security"},{"id":"NFR-DAT-001","text":"Request, assignment, negotiation and payment records must remain internally consistent.","section":"Data integrity and auditability"},{"id":"NFR-DAT-002","text":"Failed operations must not silently leave records in unintended states.","section":"Data integrity and auditability"},{"id":"NFR-DAT-003","text":"Critical changes must be traceable to the responsible user or system process.","section":"Data integrity and auditability"},{"id":"NFR-DAT-004","text":"The platform must preserve the history needed to investigate assignment and payment disputes.","section":"Data integrity and auditability"},{"id":"NFR-DAT-005","text":"Financial amounts must use appropriate precision and currency representation.","section":"Data integrity and auditability"},{"id":"NFR-REL-001","text":"Duplicate submissions and conflicting assignments must be handled safely.","section":"Reliability and performance"},{"id":"NFR-REL-002","text":"Backup and recovery procedures must be documented.","section":"Reliability and performance"},{"id":"NFR-PER-001","text":"Common operations must meet agreed response-time targets under expected load.","section":"Reliability and performance"},{"id":"NFR-PER-002","text":"The system must support growth in users, cooperatives and service requests without requiring a complete redesign.","section":"Reliability and performance"},{"id":"NFR-PER-003","text":"Reporting and analytics must not unreasonably disrupt core booking operations.","section":"Reliability and performance"},{"id":"NFR-USE-001","text":"Interfaces must present clear status descriptions and understandable actions.","section":"Usability and accessibility"},{"id":"NFR-USE-002","text":"Forms must provide clear validation feedback.","section":"Usability and accessibility"},{"id":"NFR-USE-003","text":"Core workflows must be usable on supported device sizes.","section":"Usability and accessibility"},{"id":"NFR-USE-004","text":"Language and accessibility requirements must be determined for the intended user population.","section":"Usability and accessibility"},{"id":"NFR-USE-005","text":"Customers and workers must be able to understand relevant booking, negotiation and assignment outcomes.","section":"Usability and accessibility"},{"id":"NFR-MNT-001","text":"The codebase must have clear module boundaries.","section":"Maintainability and testing"},{"id":"NFR-MNT-002","text":"Ranking and pricing rules must be testable independently of the user interface.","section":"Maintainability and testing"},{"id":"NFR-MNT-003","text":"Automated tests must cover critical workflows, authorization and business rules.","section":"Maintainability and testing"},{"id":"NFR-MNT-004","text":"Changes must be reviewed and tested before merging into the primary branch.","section":"Maintainability and testing"},{"id":"NFR-MNT-005","text":"API and data-model changes must be documented.","section":"Maintainability and testing"}],"features":[{"id":"ID-01","name":"User registration and authentication","srs":"FR-AUTH-001, 005","dependencies":"User model, authentication service","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Users can authenticate; invalid credentials are rejected."},{"id":"ID-02","name":"Role and permission management","srs":"FR-AUTH-002, 006, 007","dependencies":"ID-01, organizational model","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Users can perform only actions permitted by their assigned roles."},{"id":"ID-03","name":"Organization-scoped access","srs":"FR-AUTH-003","dependencies":"ID-02, cooperative/state records","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Users cannot access unauthorized organizations' restricted records."},{"id":"ID-04","name":"Account recovery and status management","srs":"FR-AUTH-005","dependencies":"ID-01, notification mechanism","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Recovery follows an approved process; inactive or suspended accounts cannot perform prohibited actions."},{"id":"ID-05","name":"Profile management","srs":"FR-AUTH-004","dependencies":"ID-01, role-specific profiles","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Users can update permitted profile fields and invalid updates are rejected."},{"id":"SVC-01","name":"Service categories and catalogue","srs":"FR-SVC-001, 003","dependencies":"Service data model","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Customers can browse active service categories and descriptions."},{"id":"SVC-02","name":"Cooperative service listings","srs":"FR-SVC-002, 004","dependencies":"Cooperative records, SVC-01","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Customers can identify which cooperatives offer a service; authorized managers can maintain listings."},{"id":"SVC-03","name":"Service search and filtering","srs":"FR-SVC-005","dependencies":"SVC-01, SVC-02","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Search and filters return services matching the selected criteria."},{"id":"SVC-04","name":"Pricing-type configuration","srs":"FR-SVC-006","dependencies":"SVC-01, pricing policy","priority":"P0","acceptance":"A service is identified as fixed-price, indicative-price or negotiable; the displayed price type is unambiguous."},{"id":"REQ-01","name":"Household/community service requests","srs":"FR-REQ-001–005","dependencies":"ID-01, SVC-01, SVC-02","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Valid requests are saved with a unique reference; invalid requests receive actionable errors."},{"id":"REQ-02","name":"Request review and clarification","srs":"FR-REQ-006, 007","dependencies":"REQ-01, cooperative permissions","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Authorized managers can accept a request for processing, reject it or request clarification."},{"id":"REQ-03","name":"Booking status and history","srs":"FR-REQ-008, 010","dependencies":"REQ-01, status model","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Customers can view current status and historical outcomes."},{"id":"REQ-04","name":"Cancellation and rescheduling","srs":"FR-REQ-009","dependencies":"REQ-01, status model, policy decisions","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Only permitted cancellation or rescheduling actions succeed and are recorded."},{"id":"REQ-05","name":"Customer budget input","srs":"FR-REQ-003","dependencies":"REQ-01, pricing model","priority":"P1","acceptance":"A customer can optionally supply a budget without being forced to set a fixed price."},{"id":"WRK-01","name":"Worker registration and cooperative association","srs":"FR-WRK-001–003","dependencies":"ID-01, cooperative model","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Worker profiles are linked to authorized cooperative records and follow the approved onboarding process."},{"id":"WRK-02","name":"Skills and service eligibility","srs":"FR-WRK-001, 003","dependencies":"WRK-01, service catalogue","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Managers can maintain relevant skills and eligibility; only authorized users can change approval status."},{"id":"WRK-03","name":"Availability management","srs":"FR-WRK-004, FR-WRK-011, FR-RANK-004","dependencies":"WRK-01, scheduling model","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Availability is stored with clear meaning and can be updated by authorized users; an unavailable status is not automatically a hard offer exclusion."},{"id":"WRK-04","name":"Worker work history and workload","srs":"FR-WRK-010, FR-RANK-003, 008","dependencies":"Assignment records","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Authorized users can retrieve relevant work history and workload information."},{"id":"WRK-05","name":"Worker status and eligibility lifecycle","srs":"FR-WRK-003, FR-RANK-002","dependencies":"WRK-01, WRK-02","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Ineligible workers are excluded where required by the approved eligibility rules."},{"id":"RANK-01","name":"Eligibility filtering","srs":"FR-RANK-001, 002, BR-029","dependencies":"WRK-02, WRK-03, REQ-01","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Candidates failing mandatory suitability, safety or service-eligibility requirements are excluded."},{"id":"RANK-02","name":"Worker ranking algorithm","srs":"FR-RANK-001–004","dependencies":"RANK-01, WRK-04, approved ranking policy","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Given the same inputs and policy version, the algorithm produces consistent, testable rankings."},{"id":"RANK-03","name":"Manager recommendation interface","srs":"FR-RANK-005, 006","dependencies":"RANK-02, cooperative dashboard","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Managers can review ranked eligible candidates before sending an offer."},{"id":"RANK-04","name":"Allocation history and decision records","srs":"FR-RANK-007, 008","dependencies":"RANK-02, assignment records","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Candidate recommendations and final assignment decisions can be traced according to policy."},{"id":"RANK-05","name":"Fairness monitoring","srs":"FR-RANK-009, 010","dependencies":"RANK-04, reporting","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Authorized managers can review defined allocation indicators and identify potential imbalances."},{"id":"RANK-06","name":"Manager override and justification","srs":"FR-RANK-010","dependencies":"RANK-03, audit logging","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Overrides follow the approved policy and retain the required justification and decision history."},{"id":"ASG-01","name":"Assignment offer creation","srs":"FR-ASG-001, 002","dependencies":"RANK-03, cooperative permissions","priority":"P0","acceptance":"An authorized manager can send an offer, including to a worker marked unavailable under the agreed policy."},{"id":"ASG-02","name":"Accept/reject offer","srs":"FR-WRK-006, FR-ASG-003–005","dependencies":"ASG-01, worker interface","priority":"P0","acceptance":"The worker can accept or reject; the response and timestamp are recorded."},{"id":"ASG-03","name":"Offer expiry and withdrawal","srs":"FR-ASG-004–006","dependencies":"ASG-01, timeout policy, notifications","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Expired or withdrawn offers cannot become confirmed assignments."},{"id":"ASG-04","name":"Ranked-candidate reassignment","srs":"FR-ASG-006, 007, FR-WRK-009","dependencies":"RANK-02, ASG-02, scheduling rules","priority":"P0","acceptance":"A rejected or expired offer can be followed by another eligible offer; incompatible confirmed assignments are prevented."},{"id":"ASG-05","name":"Assignment confirmation","srs":"FR-ASG-008–010","dependencies":"ASG-02, negotiation where required","priority":"P0","acceptance":"The job is confirmed only after the required worker response, customer agreement and cooperative approvals."},{"id":"NEG-01","name":"Worker quote submission","srs":"FR-NEG-001–003","dependencies":"ASG-02, SVC-04, pricing model","priority":"P0","acceptance":"A worker can propose a price and the applicable scope, schedule and payment terms."},{"id":"NEG-02","name":"Customer acceptance and counteroffer","srs":"FR-NEG-004, 005","dependencies":"NEG-01, customer interface","priority":"P0","acceptance":"A customer can accept, reject or counter a quote; the worker can respond to a counteroffer."},{"id":"NEG-03","name":"Quote version history","srs":"FR-NEG-006, 007","dependencies":"NEG-01, NEG-02","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Previous quotes and counteroffers remain retrievable; proposed and agreed prices are distinct."},{"id":"NEG-04","name":"Final agreement record","srs":"FR-NEG-008, 009","dependencies":"NEG-01, NEG-02, agreed scope model","priority":"P0","acceptance":"The final price, scope, schedule and terms are recorded only after the required parties agree."},{"id":"NEG-05","name":"Negotiation timeout and failure handling","srs":"FR-NEG-010, 011","dependencies":"NEG-01, notification and timeout policy","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Expired or failed negotiations follow a defined closure or reassignment path."},{"id":"NEG-06","name":"Scope and price change management","srs":"FR-NEG-012","dependencies":"NEG-04, audit logging","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Changes after agreement require the specified approvals and preserve the previous agreement history."},{"id":"PAY-01","name":"Payment terms and obligations","srs":"FR-PAY-001–003","dependencies":"NEG-04, payment policy","priority":"P0","acceptance":"The platform records the agreed payment terms, amounts due and outstanding balances."},{"id":"PAY-02","name":"Payment records and status tracking","srs":"FR-PAY-004, 005, 012","dependencies":"PAY-01, financial data model","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Declared, processing, confirmed, outstanding and disputed states are distinguishable."},{"id":"PAY-03","name":"Cash payment declarations","srs":"FR-PAY-005, 012","dependencies":"PAY-02, confirmation policy","priority":"P1","acceptance":"A declared cash payment is not represented as independently verified without an appropriate basis."},{"id":"PAY-04","name":"Digital payment integration","srs":"FR-PAY-006","dependencies":"PAY-01, provider selection, security review","priority":"P2","acceptance":"Provider transaction states and references are recorded; a failed transaction is not marked paid."},{"id":"PAY-05","name":"Refunds, partial payments and adjustments","srs":"FR-PAY-007","dependencies":"PAY-02, financial policy","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Authorized adjustments create traceable financial entries and correct outstanding balances."},{"id":"PAY-06","name":"Financial disputes and reconciliation","srs":"FR-PAY-008, 009","dependencies":"PAY-02, complaint workflow","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Disputes are tracked to resolution and financial history remains auditable."},{"id":"PAY-07","name":"Cooperative fees and settlement rules","srs":"FR-PAY-010, 011","dependencies":"Payment recipient and fee policy","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Charges and revenue-sharing calculations follow a documented, authorized policy."},{"id":"JOB-01","name":"Worker job dashboard","srs":"FR-JOB-001","dependencies":"ASG-05, worker permissions","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Workers can view confirmed jobs and relevant service details."},{"id":"JOB-02","name":"Job status updates","srs":"FR-JOB-002, 003","dependencies":"JOB-01, status model","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Authorized status transitions are recorded with timestamps."},{"id":"JOB-03","name":"Delays and inability to complete","srs":"FR-JOB-004, 009","dependencies":"JOB-01, notification workflow","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Workers can report issues and the cooperative receives the required update."},{"id":"JOB-04","name":"Completion evidence and verification","srs":"FR-JOB-005–008, FR-JOB-011","dependencies":"JOB-02, completion policy","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Completion records and permitted post-confirmation assignment information are visible to authorized parties."},{"id":"JOB-05","name":"Ratings and feedback","srs":"FR-JOB-010","dependencies":"JOB-04, customer interface","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Permitted feedback can be submitted and linked to the relevant completed service."},{"id":"JOB-06","name":"Complaints and service disputes","srs":"FR-JOB-010, FR-DSP-001–006","dependencies":"JOB-04, complaint policy","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Issues can be recorded, assigned for review, escalated and closed with a traceable outcome."},{"id":"COOP-01","name":"Cooperative profile and service management","srs":"FR-COOP-001, 002","dependencies":"ID-03, SVC-01","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Authorized managers can maintain only their cooperative's permitted records."},{"id":"COOP-02","name":"Request and workforce operations dashboard","srs":"FR-COOP-003–006","dependencies":"REQ-02, WRK-01, RANK-03, ASG-01","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Managers can review requests, manage offers and monitor active jobs from their operational view."},{"id":"COOP-03","name":"Operational exception handling","srs":"FR-COOP-007, 008","dependencies":"ASG-04, JOB-03, JOB-06","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Managers can process reassignment, complaints and service issues within their permissions."},{"id":"COOP-04","name":"Cooperative reporting","srs":"FR-COOP-009","dependencies":"Request, worker, assignment and job records","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Managers can view accurate reports limited to their cooperative's scope."},{"id":"ADM-01","name":"Central platform monitoring","srs":"FR-ADM-001, 002, 008","dependencies":"Audit records, reporting and scope permissions","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Authorized central administrators can review platform-level indicators without automatically gaining unrestricted operational access."},{"id":"ADM-02","name":"State cooperative registration and management","srs":"FR-ADM-003–005","dependencies":"ID-03, organizational model","priority":"P0","acceptance":"State administrators can register and manage cooperatives within their authorized scope."},{"id":"ADM-03","name":"Administrative audit and escalation","srs":"FR-ADM-006, 007, 010","dependencies":"Role model, audit logging","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Administrative actions are attributable and issues can be escalated to the authorized level."},{"id":"ADM-04","name":"Shared policy management","srs":"FR-ADM-009, FR-ADM-011","dependencies":"Governance approval model","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Changes to common policies are authorized and traceable to the responsible actor, effective time and policy version."},{"id":"INS-01","name":"Institutional account and representative authorization","srs":"FR-INS-001, FR-INS-009","dependencies":"ID-01, organizational model","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Full-platform feature: only authorized representatives can submit requests for their institution and maintain permitted organization/contact information. Deferred from MVP."},{"id":"INS-02","name":"Institutional requirement submission","srs":"FR-INS-002–004","dependencies":"INS-01, REQ-02","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Full-platform feature: institutions can submit requirements; cooperatives can review and record a decision. Deferred from MVP."},{"id":"INS-03","name":"Institutional delivery tracking","srs":"FR-INS-005–007, FR-INS-010, FR-INS-011","dependencies":"INS-02, ASG-05, JOB-02, JOB-04","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Full-platform feature: accepted institutional requests can be assigned, monitored and closed; authorized representatives can access scoped service reports and conditional financial records. Deferred from MVP."},{"id":"INS-04","name":"Contract, tender and procurement management","srs":"FR-INS-008","dependencies":"Institutional policy, agreement model","priority":"P2","acceptance":"Conditional full-platform feature: if stakeholder validation approves it, authorized users can manage the defined contract lifecycle and associated records. Outside MVP."},{"id":"NOT-01","name":"Booking and job notifications","srs":"FR-NOT-001, 005","dependencies":"Status-change events, notification service","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Relevant parties receive updates after specified status changes."},{"id":"NOT-02","name":"Assignment offer notifications","srs":"FR-NOT-002, 004","dependencies":"ASG-01, ASG-02, notification service","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Workers receive offer notifications and response outcomes are reflected accurately."},{"id":"NOT-03","name":"Negotiation notifications","srs":"FR-NOT-003","dependencies":"NEG-01, NEG-02, notification service","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Relevant parties are notified of new quotes and counteroffers."},{"id":"NOT-04","name":"Payment and complaint notifications","srs":"FR-NOT-005, 006","dependencies":"PAY-02, JOB-06, notification service","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Relevant parties receive permitted updates, and delivery status is recorded where supported."},{"id":"REP-01","name":"Service operations reporting","srs":"FR-REP-001","dependencies":"Request, assignment and job records","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Authorized users can review request volumes and service outcomes."},{"id":"REP-02","name":"Workforce utilization reporting","srs":"FR-REP-002","dependencies":"WRK-04, assignment history","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Reports reflect recorded workload and assignment history."},{"id":"REP-03","name":"Fair allocation analytics","srs":"FR-REP-003","dependencies":"RANK-04, RANK-05","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Reports expose the approved fairness indicators and relevant time periods."},{"id":"REP-04","name":"State and platform reporting","srs":"FR-REP-004, 005","dependencies":"ADM-01, ADM-02, data access policies","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Reports respect state and platform-level permissions."},{"id":"REP-05","name":"Financial reporting","srs":"FR-REP-006, 007","dependencies":"PAY-01–PAY-07","priority":"P2","acceptance":"Authorized reports reconcile with recorded financial events and respect data boundaries."},{"id":"PLT-01","name":"Backend authorization enforcement","srs":"NFR-SEC-001–003","dependencies":"ID-02, ID-03","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Direct API requests cannot bypass role or organization-level restrictions."},{"id":"PLT-02","name":"Audit trail","srs":"FR-RANK-007, FR-ADM-007, NFR-DAT-003, 004","dependencies":"Identity model, critical domain events","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Important decisions and changes retain actor, time and relevant outcome information."},{"id":"PLT-03","name":"Data validation and integrity","srs":"NFR-SEC-005, NFR-DAT-001, 002","dependencies":"API and domain validation","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Invalid inputs and failed operations do not silently create inconsistent records."},{"id":"PLT-04","name":"Duplicate and concurrency protection","srs":"NFR-REL-001","dependencies":"Request/assignment data model, transactional operations","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Duplicate submissions and concurrent assignment attempts are handled safely."},{"id":"PLT-05","name":"Backup and recovery","srs":"NFR-REL-002","dependencies":"Database and deployment infrastructure","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Documented backup and restore procedures can be tested."},{"id":"PLT-06","name":"Automated testing and CI","srs":"NFR-SEC-006, NFR-MNT-002–004","dependencies":"Repository and test framework","priority":"P0","acceptance":"Automated checks run on changes and cover critical business rules."},{"id":"PLT-07","name":"API and architecture documentation","srs":"NFR-MNT-001, 005","dependencies":"Architecture and API design","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Interfaces and material data-model changes are documented."},{"id":"PLT-08","name":"Performance and scaling controls","srs":"NFR-PER-001–003","dependencies":"Architecture, load assumptions","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Performance tests can evaluate agreed targets under expected load."},{"id":"PLT-09","name":"Accessibility and responsive interface","srs":"NFR-USE-001–005","dependencies":"Frontend design system","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Core workflows are usable across supported screen sizes and meet agreed accessibility criteria."},{"id":"PLT-10","name":"Privacy and data lifecycle controls","srs":"NFR-SEC-006, NFR-SEC-007","dependencies":"Data classification, retention policy","priority":"P1","acceptance":"Data access and lifecycle actions follow approved privacy, retention, correction and deletion policies."},{"id":"FUT-01","name":"Advanced demand forecasting","srs":"Extended platform scope","dependencies":"Sufficient historical data, validated forecasting need","priority":"P2","acceptance":"Forecasts are evaluated against an agreed baseline and their limitations are documented."},{"id":"FUT-02","name":"Advanced recommendation optimization","srs":"Extended platform scope","dependencies":"RANK-02, reliable outcome data, evaluation criteria","priority":"P2","acceptance":"Any enhanced ranking approach is compared against the existing rules using approved evaluation measures."},{"id":"FUT-03","name":"External welfare, insurance or support integrations","srs":"Extended platform scope","dependencies":"Partner availability, legal and security review","priority":"P2","acceptance":"Approved integrations meet defined access, consent, security and data-exchange requirements."},{"id":"FUT-04","name":"Dedicated Android application","srs":"Extended platform scope","dependencies":"Stable API contracts, client requirements","priority":"P2","acceptance":"The mobile client supports the approved mobile workflows through authorized APIs."},{"id":"FUT-05","name":"Advanced analytics and dashboards","srs":"FR-REP-001–007","dependencies":"Reliable operational data, reporting requirements","priority":"P2","acceptance":"Dashboards present validated metrics with appropriate access controls and definitions."}],"mvp":{"ID-01":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Authenticate individual customers, workers and authorized cooperative users.","acceptance":"Valid users authenticate; invalid credentials are rejected."},"ID-02":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Implement customer, worker and cooperative-manager permissions; retain extensible administrative roles.","acceptance":"A user cannot perform an action outside the assigned role."},"ID-03":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Enforce cooperative-level isolation for every MVP request, worker, assignment and payment record.","acceptance":"A user cannot retrieve another cooperative’s restricted records."},"ID-04":{"classification":"Should","scope":"Provide recovery and inactive/suspended account controls; recovery-channel details remain policy-dependent.","acceptance":"A recovery request follows the approved process, and a prohibited action by an inactive/suspended account is rejected."},"ID-05":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Support permitted customer, worker and cooperative-user profile fields.","acceptance":"Permitted profile changes succeed; invalid or unauthorized changes fail."},"SVC-01":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Provide active household and community services with descriptions and requirements.","acceptance":"An individual customer can browse active services and requirements."},"SVC-02":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Show which cooperatives offer each service; allow authorized managers to maintain listings.","acceptance":"A customer can identify an offering cooperative."},"SVC-03":{"classification":"Should","scope":"Provide practical location/category filtering where data is reliable.","acceptance":"A selected filter returns matching services."},"SVC-04":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Distinguish fixed, indicative and negotiable service pricing.","acceptance":"The displayed pricing type is unambiguous."},"REQ-01":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Support individual-customer requests with service, location, schedule and description.","acceptance":"A valid request receives a unique reference; invalid input is rejected."},"REQ-02":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Allow a cooperative manager to accept, reject or request clarification.","acceptance":"Each manager decision is recorded with status and actor."},"REQ-03":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Expose current and historical individual-customer request outcomes.","acceptance":"A customer can view current status and prior outcomes."},"REQ-04":{"classification":"Should","scope":"Support policy-approved requests and recorded outcomes; exact policy remains open.","acceptance":"An unauthorized cancellation is rejected; an allowed action is traceable."},"REQ-05":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Capture an optional budget without forcing a fixed price.","acceptance":"Budget input does not make a negotiable service fixed-price."},"WRK-01":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Onboard and associate workers with the authorized cooperative.","acceptance":"An approved worker is linked to the correct cooperative."},"WRK-02":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Maintain skills, eligibility and mandatory service/safety information.","acceptance":"Only authorized users can change eligibility."},"WRK-03":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Maintain availability as a ranking/scheduling input; it is not an automatic offer exclusion.","acceptance":"An unavailable worker may receive an offer under the approved workflow."},"WRK-04":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Retain assignment and workload data needed for fair allocation.","acceptance":"Authorized users can retrieve relevant history."},"WRK-05":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Apply approved inactive, suspended and eligibility states.","acceptance":"Ineligible workers are excluded where rules require it."},"RANK-01":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Exclude workers failing mandatory suitability, safety or service-eligibility requirements.","acceptance":"Mandatory failures are excluded and recorded."},"RANK-02":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Use deterministic, documented ranking with suitability, workload, previous allocations and availability factors.","acceptance":"Equivalent inputs and policy versions produce reproducible rankings."},"RANK-03":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Let managers review ranked candidates before sending offers.","acceptance":"A manager can review eligible ranked candidates."},"RANK-04":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Record recommendations, selected worker, rationale and policy version.","acceptance":"Allocation decisions are traceable."},"RANK-05":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Provide the approved indicators for reviewing opportunity distribution.","acceptance":"Authorized users can inspect defined fairness indicators."},"RANK-06":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Permit only policy-approved overrides with justification and audit history.","acceptance":"An override without required justification is rejected."},"ASG-01":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Managers send offers to selected workers, including unavailable workers where permitted.","acceptance":"An authorized manager can send an offer."},"ASG-02":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Workers accept or reject offers; responses and timestamps are retained.","acceptance":"Accepted and rejected offers cannot be confused with confirmed assignments."},"ASG-03":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Implement the offer expiry/withdrawal state required for recovery and ranked-candidate reassignment; timeout duration remains an open policy decision.","acceptance":"An expired or withdrawn offer cannot become confirmed, and its terminal state can trigger the approved reassignment path."},"ASG-04":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Offer another eligible ranked candidate after rejection/expiry and prevent conflicts.","acceptance":"Reassignment follows eligibility and conflict rules."},"ASG-05":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Confirm only after worker response, required customer agreement, cooperative approval and conflict checks.","acceptance":"A recommendation or offer alone never creates a confirmed assignment."},"NEG-01":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Support quotes for services without predefined fixed prices.","acceptance":"A quote records amount, scope, schedule and terms."},"NEG-02":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Support customer accept/reject/counteroffer and worker response.","acceptance":"Counteroffers and responses are recorded."},"NEG-03":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Preserve every quote and counteroffer; distinguish proposed from agreed price.","acceptance":"Prior versions remain retrievable."},"NEG-04":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Record agreed scope, schedule, price and payment terms before confirmation.","acceptance":"The agreement is created only after required parties accept the same terms."},"NEG-05":{"classification":"Should","scope":"Support approved timeout, closure or reassignment behavior.","acceptance":"Failed negotiation follows a defined path."},"NEG-06":{"classification":"Should","scope":"Record approved post-agreement changes and preserve prior versions.","acceptance":"An unapproved scope/price change is rejected."},"PAY-01":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Record agreed terms, amounts due and balances for individual-customer jobs.","acceptance":"Agreed payment obligations are retrievable."},"PAY-02":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Record declared, processing, confirmed, outstanding and disputed states without gateway claims.","acceptance":"Statuses remain distinguishable."},"PAY-03":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Record cash declarations without representing them as independently verified.","acceptance":"A cash declaration does not become verified without evidence."},"PAY-05":{"classification":"Should","scope":"Record approved adjustments and partial payments.","acceptance":"Balances update with traceable entries."},"PAY-06":{"classification":"Should","scope":"Track individual-customer payment disputes and resolutions.","acceptance":"A dispute has an attributable resolution history."},"PAY-07":{"classification":"Conditional","scope":"Requires an approved fee, revenue-sharing and settlement policy; no calculation is enabled in MVP by default.","acceptance":""},"COOP-01":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Maintain cooperative profile and service listings within scope.","acceptance":"Managers cannot edit another cooperative’s records."},"COOP-02":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Provide the manager view for requests, recommendations, offers and active jobs.","acceptance":"A manager can operate the complete individual-customer workflow."},"COOP-03":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Support basic reassignment and failed-assignment handling; complaints and broader service issues remain reduced-scope extensions.","acceptance":"An authorized manager can record a failed assignment and initiate an eligible reassignment; broader complaint handling follows approved policy where enabled."},"COOP-04":{"classification":"Should","scope":"Provide basic request, assignment, completion and workforce summaries.","acceptance":"Reports are limited to the cooperative scope."},"JOB-01":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Show confirmed individual-customer jobs and service details.","acceptance":"Workers can view confirmed jobs."},"JOB-02":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Support permitted progress transitions and timestamps.","acceptance":"Invalid transitions are rejected."},"JOB-03":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Let workers report inability or delay so the cooperative can recover through reassignment; broader exception workflows remain policy-dependent.","acceptance":"A failed-assignment report is recorded, visible to the cooperative and eligible for the approved reassignment path."},"JOB-04":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Record and verify individual-customer completion; expose permitted assignment information.","acceptance":"Completion follows the approved verification process."},"JOB-05":{"classification":"Later","scope":"Valuable service-quality capability, but not required to complete the core workflow.","acceptance":""},"JOB-06":{"classification":"Should","scope":"Record and resolve individual-customer issues separately from booking status.","acceptance":"Issues are attributable, escalatable and closable."},"ADM-03":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Implement minimum administrative audit and escalation needed for cooperative operations.","acceptance":"Administrative actions identify actor, time and outcome."},"ADM-01":{"classification":"Should","scope":"Provide limited authorized oversight/aggregates only; broad platform reporting is deferred.","acceptance":"Central access cannot bypass cooperative isolation."},"ADM-02":{"classification":"Later","scope":"Preserve the multi-tenant model but defer broad state workflows from the pilot MVP.","acceptance":"Later implementation remains scoped to authorized states."},"ADM-04":{"classification":"Conditional","scope":"Requires approved policy authority and versioning before implementation.","acceptance":"No shared policy change becomes effective without approved control."},"NOT-01":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Notify individual customers, workers and managers of core status changes.","acceptance":"Core request, assignment, completion and payment updates are delivered."},"NOT-02":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Notify workers of offers and responses.","acceptance":"Offer and response outcomes are accurately reflected."},"NOT-03":{"classification":"Should","scope":"Notify customers/workers of quotes and counteroffers.","acceptance":"Relevant parties receive negotiation updates."},"NOT-04":{"classification":"Should","scope":"Notify individual-customer parties of permitted payment and complaint changes.","acceptance":"Notification delivery status is retained where supported."},"REP-01":{"classification":"Should","scope":"Provide basic individual-customer request and completion summaries.","acceptance":"Authorized users can review request volumes and outcomes."},"REP-02":{"classification":"Should","scope":"Provide basic recorded workload summaries.","acceptance":"Reports match recorded workload data."},"REP-03":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Provide the approved fairness indicators required to review MVP allocation.","acceptance":"Authorized users can inspect allocation indicators."},"REP-04":{"classification":"Later","scope":"Defer broad state/platform reports while retaining access-boundary design.","acceptance":"No deferred report is exposed as an MVP capability."},"REP-05":{"classification":"Conditional","scope":"Defer until payment and settlement policies are approved.","acceptance":"Financial reports are not enabled without approved policy and permissions."},"PLT-01":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Enforce role and cooperative boundaries on every API.","acceptance":"Direct API calls cannot bypass restrictions."},"PLT-02":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Audit material allocation, assignment, administrative, negotiation and payment events.","acceptance":"Material decisions retain actor, time and outcome."},"PLT-03":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Validate domain inputs and prevent unintended partial states.","acceptance":"Invalid operations do not create inconsistent records."},"PLT-04":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Protect requests, offers, confirmations and payment records from duplicates/conflicts.","acceptance":"Concurrent assignment attempts are handled safely."},"PLT-05":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Establish and verify basic backup/restore for the MVP deployment.","acceptance":"A documented restore procedure succeeds in a test."},"PLT-06":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Test authorization, allocation, state transitions and critical workflows automatically.","acceptance":"Automated checks run and cover critical business rules."},"PLT-07":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Document the MVP interfaces and material data-model decisions.","acceptance":"Core interfaces and changes are documented."},"PLT-08":{"classification":"Should","scope":"Test agreed pilot targets; quantitative targets remain an open decision.","acceptance":"Performance tests evaluate approved targets."},"PLT-09":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Provide responsive web workflows and a documented baseline accessibility check.","acceptance":"Core workflows work on supported screen sizes."},"PLT-10":{"classification":"Must","scope":"Apply approved access, retention, correction and deletion controls.","acceptance":"Lifecycle actions follow approved policies."},"INS-01":{"classification":"Later","scope":"Institutional customers are outside MVP; retain for the full platform.","acceptance":""},"INS-02":{"classification":"Later","scope":"Institutional requests are outside MVP.","acceptance":""},"INS-03":{"classification":"Later","scope":"Institutional tracking, reports and conditional financial visibility are outside MVP.","acceptance":""},"INS-04":{"classification":"Conditional","scope":"Requires stakeholder validation; remains outside MVP.","acceptance":""},"PAY-04":{"classification":"Later","scope":"Gateway processing is excluded from MVP.","acceptance":""},"FUT-01":{"classification":"Later","scope":"Requires historical data and validated need.","acceptance":""},"FUT-02":{"classification":"Later","scope":"Transparent baseline ranking is sufficient for MVP.","acceptance":""},"FUT-03":{"classification":"Conditional","scope":"Requires partners, legal basis and security review.","acceptance":""},"FUT-04":{"classification":"Later","scope":"The initial release is web-first.","acceptance":""},"FUT-05":{"classification":"Later","scope":"Defer until metrics and data volume justify it.","acceptance":""}},"sourceText":{"scope":"# Cooperative GIG — Project Scope\n**Version:** v0.1  \n**Document type:** Project Scope  \n**Status:** Working Draft — Pending Validation\n\n## 1. Problem Statement\n\nLabour cooperative societies have skilled workers who can provide household, community and institutional services. However, customers need a structured and reliable way to discover these services, submit requests, coordinate with cooperatives and track service delivery.\n\nCooperative societies also need effective digital tools to manage their workforce, maintain worker profiles, monitor availability, coordinate assignments and ensure accountability. Without transparent allocation processes, suitable workers may not receive equitable opportunities to access available jobs.\n\nCooperative GIG aims to address these challenges through a cooperative-oriented digital platform that connects customers with cooperative-associated workers while supporting workforce management, service coordination, fair job allocation and accountable service delivery.\n\nThe platform is intended to operate through a centralized digital system with state-level administration and society-level operations. It will provide a common environment in which customers can request services, workers can manage their work-related information, cooperatives can coordinate service delivery, and authorized administrators can oversee operations within their respective responsibilities.\n\nThe long-term platform vision extends beyond booking management. It may also encompass institutional service coordination, financial transactions, operational reporting, performance monitoring and additional digital services as the platform's requirements mature. These capabilities will be validated and documented before the implementation scope is finalized.\n\n## 2. Project Objectives\n\n1. **Service discovery and access:** Enable customers to discover available services and submit household, community or institutional service requests through a structured digital platform.\n\n2. **Cooperative workforce management:** Enable cooperative societies to maintain worker profiles, manage skills and availability, organize their workforce and coordinate service delivery.\n\n3. **Transparent job allocation:** Establish clear, consistent and auditable rules for recommending eligible workers and confirming assignments.\n\n4. **Equitable work opportunities:** Design job-allocation mechanisms that seek to distribute suitable work opportunities fairly among eligible workers, taking account of relevant factors such as availability, skills, workload and previous allocations.\n\n5. **Service lifecycle visibility:** Provide appropriate visibility into requests, booking decisions, worker assignments, job progress, completion and related records.\n\n6. **Multi-level administration:** Support a centralized platform with authorized state-level administration and society-level operational management.\n\n7. **Accountability and governance:** Maintain appropriate records of important decisions and actions to support operational oversight, dispute investigation and responsible platform administration.\n\n8. **Worker and customer support:** Provide appropriate processes for profile management, booking changes, cancellations, complaints, feedback and other service-related interactions.\n\n9. **Institutional service coordination:** Support organizations that require services from cooperative societies, including requirements submission, workforce coordination and service-delivery monitoring.\n\n10. **Operational efficiency:** Reduce manual coordination, improve access to relevant information and help cooperatives manage service requests and workforce utilization more effectively.\n\n11. **Secure and reliable operation:** Protect user information, enforce role-based permissions, preserve data integrity and provide a maintainable foundation for future platform growth.\n\n12. **Extensibility:** Establish a platform architecture that can accommodate additional services, financial capabilities, reporting tools and client applications as requirements and resources permit.\n\n## 3. Platform Scope\n\nThis section describes the intended capability areas of Cooperative GIG as a complete platform. It is not the final Version 1 feature list. Individual capabilities, business rules and dependencies remain subject to requirements validation.\n\n### 3.1 User Accounts and Access Management\n\n- User registration, authentication and account management.\n- Role-based access for customers, workers, cooperative managers, state administrators and platform administrators.\n- Support for institutional accounts and authorized institutional representatives.\n- Profile maintenance and account-status management.\n- Permission boundaries based on role and organizational responsibility.\n- Account verification and approval processes, where required.\n- Secure account recovery and session management.\n\n### 3.2 Service Catalogue and Discovery\n\n- A centralized catalogue of services offered through participating cooperatives.\n- Service categories, descriptions, requirements and relevant service information.\n- Discovery and filtering of services based on relevant criteria, such as location and service category.\n- Visibility into the cooperatives providing particular services.\n- Availability information where it can be reliably maintained.\n- Service-specific requirements and eligibility conditions.\n- Management of service listings by authorized personnel.\n\n### 3.3 Worker Profiles and Workforce Management\n\n- Worker registration or onboarding through an authorized process.\n- Worker profiles containing relevant skills, experience, service capabilities and other approved information.\n- Worker verification and approval workflows.\n- Association of workers with their respective cooperative societies.\n- Management of worker availability and work-related status.\n- Maintenance of worker skills, qualifications and service eligibility.\n- Visibility into current assignments and relevant work history.\n- Worker profile updates and changes to eligibility or participation status.\n- Workforce reports for authorized cooperative and administrative users.\n\n### 3.4 Customer Service Requests and Bookings\n\n- Submission of household and community service requests.\n- Selection of a service and the relevant cooperative, where applicable.\n- Collection of required service details, location, preferred schedule and other relevant information.\n- Request review, acceptance, rejection or requests for clarification by authorized personnel.\n- Booking confirmation and status notifications.\n- Viewing of current and historical requests.\n- Cancellation and rescheduling according to defined policies.\n- Handling of unavailable services, incomplete requests and other booking exceptions.\n- Feedback and service ratings, subject to the platform's approved policies.\n\n### 3.5 Institutional Service Management\n\n- Institutional account onboarding and authorization.\n- Submission of service requirements by eligible organizations.\n- Recording of service scope, workforce requirements, location, schedule and other relevant details.\n- Review and clarification of institutional requests.\n- Assessment of workforce availability and cooperative capacity.\n- Coordination between institutions and authorized cooperative representatives.\n- Monitoring of accepted institutional service requests and their progress.\n- Recording of delivery outcomes and completion evidence.\n- Support for more comprehensive institutional agreements and contracts if validated as part of the long-term platform.\n\n### 3.6 Cooperative Management and Operations\n\n- Cooperative profile and service-catalogue management.\n- Worker onboarding, verification and profile administration.\n- Workforce availability and capacity management.\n- Review and coordination of incoming service requests.\n- Worker eligibility assessment and assignment management.\n- Monitoring of active jobs and service-delivery status.\n- Reassignment and exception handling.\n- Maintenance of operational records and relevant history.\n- Reporting on requests, assignments, completion and workforce utilization.\n- Management of authorized cooperative personnel and their permissions.\n\n### 3.7 Fair Worker Allocation\n\n- Identification of workers who meet the requirements of a service request.\n- Filtering based on skills, availability, service eligibility, location and other approved criteria.\n- Recommendation of suitable workers using transparent and documented rules.\n- Consideration of workload and previous job allocations to support equitable access to opportunities.\n- Review and confirmation of assignments by an authorized cooperative manager.\n- Recording of assignment decisions and relevant reasons.\n- Prevention of conflicting assignments where applicable.\n- Reassignment when a worker becomes unavailable or a job cannot proceed.\n- Monitoring of allocation patterns to identify potential imbalances.\n- Periodic review of allocation rules and their effects on worker opportunity distribution.\n\nFairness will be treated as an explicit business requirement, rather than assumed to result automatically from automated recommendations. The precise allocation formula, eligibility rules, tie-breaking method and fairness measurements must be defined and validated.\n\n### 3.8 Job Execution and Completion\n\n- Visibility of assignments to the relevant workers.\n- Access to the information needed to perform an assigned job.\n- Job acceptance or acknowledgement processes, if required by the approved workflow.\n- Worker updates for job progress and status.\n- Recording of delays, inability to complete work and other exceptions.\n- Submission of completion information or supporting evidence where required.\n- Completion review or verification by an authorized party.\n- Recording of final job status and relevant timestamps.\n- Customer or institutional confirmation and feedback, where applicable.\n- Retention of service and assignment history for authorized users.\n\n### 3.9 Central and State-Level Administration\n\n- Central administration of authorized platform-wide settings and policies.\n- Management of state-level administrative accounts and permissions.\n- State-scoped oversight of participating cooperatives and relevant operations.\n- Management of organizational records and authorization boundaries.\n- Monitoring of operational activity and platform-level indicators.\n- Administration of approved service categories and common business rules.\n- Audit trails for significant administrative actions.\n- Escalation and investigation processes for issues requiring broader oversight.\n\nThe precise division of responsibilities between central administrators and state administrators remains subject to governance validation.\n\n### 3.10 Notifications and Communication\n\n- Notifications for request submission, review, assignment and status changes.\n- Communication of relevant booking decisions to customers and institutions.\n- Assignment and job-update notifications for workers.\n- Notifications for cancellations, rescheduling and exceptions.\n- Administrative alerts for relevant operational issues.\n- In-platform communication or messaging, if required.\n- Support for additional notification channels as appropriate.\n\n### 3.11 Financial and Settlement Capabilities\n\n- Recording of approved service charges and pricing information.\n- Support for payment tracking and transaction records.\n- Integration with payment providers if online payments are adopted.\n- Recording of refunds, cancellations, adjustments and related financial events where applicable.\n- Cooperative-level settlement and financial reporting.\n- Reconciliation and audit records for financial transactions.\n\nThe platform's pricing model, payment recipient, distribution of earnings, fees, settlement process and responsibility for financial disputes must be defined before these capabilities are specified in detail.\n\n### 3.12 Feedback, Complaints and Dispute Handling\n\n- Collection of customer feedback and service ratings.\n- Recording of service-related complaints.\n- Assignment of complaints to authorized personnel.\n- Tracking of investigation and resolution status.\n- Recording of decisions and supporting information.\n- Escalation of unresolved issues according to defined governance rules.\n- Review of feedback and complaints to identify recurring operational problems.\n\n### 3.13 Reporting and Analytics\n\n- Reports on service requests, bookings and job completion.\n- Workforce availability and utilization reporting.\n- Analysis of allocation patterns and distribution of work opportunities.\n- Cooperative-level operational reports.\n- State-level oversight reports.\n- Platform-level performance indicators for authorized administrators.\n- Institutional service-delivery reports.\n- Financial reports if financial functionality is introduced.\n- Data exports and advanced analytics where authorized and appropriate.\n\nReporting must respect organizational access boundaries and protect sensitive worker and customer information.\n\n### 3.14 Security, Privacy and Auditability\n\n- Authentication and role-based authorization.\n- Protection of personal, organizational and service-related data.\n- Validation of incoming data and controlled state transitions.\n- Secure management of application secrets and credentials.\n- Audit logging of significant actions and decisions.\n- Restrictions on access to records outside a user's authorized scope.\n- Appropriate retention, correction and deletion policies.\n- Backup, recovery and operational monitoring.\n- Security testing and handling of identified vulnerabilities.\n- Compliance with applicable legal and regulatory requirements, as determined during validation.\n\n### 3.15 Platform Interfaces and Technical Extensibility\n\n- A web-based interface for core platform users.\n- Responsive access for different screen sizes and device types.\n- API support for communication between the client and backend services.\n- Potential support for a dedicated Android application.\n- Integration interfaces for approved external services.\n- Maintainable modular architecture.\n- Automated testing and controlled deployment processes.\n- Future expansion to additional cooperatives, states, services and user groups.\n\n## 4. Primary Actors\n\n| Actor | Main responsibilities |\n|---|---|\n| Customer | Discover services, submit requests, manage bookings, track jobs and provide feedback. |\n| Institutional Customer | Submit organizational service requirements, coordinate with cooperatives and review delivery outcomes. |\n| Worker | Maintain relevant profile information, manage availability where authorized, view assignments, perform jobs and update progress. |\n| Cooperative Manager | Manage the cooperative's workforce and services, review requests, confirm worker assignments and oversee delivery. |\n| State Administrator | Administer authorized state-level operations, oversee relevant cooperatives and review state-scoped information. |\n| Platform Administrator | Manage authorized platform-wide settings, governance controls, access policies and operational oversight. |\n| Additional Authorized Personnel | Perform specific functions such as verification, support, complaint handling or financial administration if separate responsibilities are required. |\n\nAdditional personnel may be represented as separate roles or permissions within an existing role. This decision will depend on the validated operating model.\n\nThe platform must distinguish between a person's account, their organizational affiliation, their role and the permissions granted to that role. A worker's association with a cooperative does not automatically establish employment status or ownership of the platform.\n\n## 5. Core Business Workflows\n\n### 5.1 Customer Household or Community Service Workflow\n\n1. The customer accesses the platform and discovers available services.\n2. The customer selects a service and provides the required request details.\n3. The customer selects a cooperative where required by the service workflow.\n4. The system validates the request and records it.\n5. The relevant cooperative receives the request for review.\n6. An authorized cooperative manager reviews the request and assesses its requirements.\n7. The system identifies eligible workers and recommends suitable candidates according to the approved allocation rules.\n8. The cooperative manager reviews the recommendations and confirms an assignment.\n9. The customer receives the relevant booking and assignment updates.\n10. The worker performs the service and updates its progress.\n11. The service is marked complete after the required completion process.\n12. The final status is recorded, and feedback or related follow-up is collected where applicable.\n\n### 5.2 Worker Onboarding and Management Workflow\n\n1. A worker's details are submitted through the approved onboarding process.\n2. The relevant cooperative or authorized personnel review the submitted information.\n3. Required verification and approval checks are completed.\n4. The worker's cooperative association, skills and service eligibility are recorded.\n5. The worker's profile becomes available for relevant operational use after approval.\n6. The worker's availability and profile information are maintained over time.\n7. Assignments, completion records and relevant work history are updated as jobs progress.\n8. Changes in eligibility or participation status affect future recommendations and assignments according to defined rules.\n\n### 5.3 Fair Job Allocation Workflow\n\n1. A cooperative receives an accepted or reviewable service request.\n2. The system determines the request's service, skill, schedule and other eligibility requirements.\n3. The system filters out workers who do not meet mandatory requirements.\n4. Eligible workers are assessed using the approved recommendation and fairness rules.\n5. Relevant factors, such as current workload and previous opportunities, are considered where appropriate.\n6. The system presents suitable worker recommendations to an authorized cooperative manager.\n7. The manager confirms an eligible assignment or records an appropriate exception.\n8. The system records the decision and updates the worker's assignment status.\n9. The allocation history is retained for oversight and fairness analysis.\n10. Allocation outcomes are periodically reviewed to identify systematic imbalances or unintended effects.\n\n### 5.4 Institutional Service Workflow\n\n1. An authorized institutional representative submits a service requirement.\n2. The platform records the request and required service details.\n3. The relevant cooperative reviews the requirement and assesses its capacity.\n4. The institution and cooperative clarify the scope, schedule or workforce requirements where necessary.\n5. The cooperative accepts, declines or requests changes to the proposed service.\n6. Following acceptance, the cooperative organizes the required workforce and confirms assignments.\n7. The service is delivered and monitored through the platform.\n8. Completion is recorded and reviewed according to the applicable verification process.\n9. The institution and cooperative can access the relevant service records.\n10. Financial settlement, contractual closure or further follow-up occurs if those capabilities are supported and applicable.\n\n### 5.5 Cooperative Operations Workflow\n\n1. An authorized cooperative manager maintains the cooperative's profile, services and worker records.\n2. Incoming requests are reviewed and prioritized according to defined business rules.\n3. The manager assesses service feasibility and workforce availability.\n4. Eligible workers are recommended and assignments are confirmed.\n5. The manager monitors active work and addresses delays, cancellations or other exceptions.\n6. Completed jobs and related operational records are reviewed.\n7. The cooperative uses available reports to assess service delivery and workforce utilization.\n8. Significant decisions and exceptions remain traceable through the platform's records.\n\n### 5.6 Central and State Administration Workflow\n\n1. The central platform establishes authorized platform-wide policies and administrative controls.\n2. State administrators access the functions and records permitted for their scope.\n3. Authorized state administrators oversee relevant cooperative operations.\n4. Cooperative managers manage local workforce and service-delivery activities.\n5. Administrative actions and changes to important records are logged where required.\n6. Issues requiring broader intervention are escalated to the appropriate administrative level.\n7. Oversight reports are produced according to role permissions and data-access rules.\n\n### 5.7 Cancellation, Reassignment and Exception Workflow\n\n1. A customer, worker or authorized manager initiates a permitted cancellation or reports an operational issue.\n2. The platform validates the request against the applicable business rules.\n3. The affected parties receive the relevant status update.\n4. If the service remains viable, the cooperative assesses whether rescheduling or reassignment is appropriate.\n5. Any replacement assignment is made using the same eligibility and fairness requirements.\n6. The platform records the reason, decision and resulting status.\n7. Complaints, disputes or unresolved exceptions are escalated according to the approved process.\n\n## 6. Business Rules and Governance\n\n### 6.1 Role and Organizational Boundaries\n\n- Each user must have an authenticated identity before accessing protected functionality.\n- Users may perform only actions permitted by their assigned roles and organizational scope.\n- Cooperative managers must not automatically gain access to another cooperative's restricted records.\n- State administrators must operate within their authorized state-level scope.\n- Platform-wide access must be restricted to explicitly authorized administrative functions.\n- Institutional access must be limited to the institution's permitted requests and related records.\n\n### 6.2 Worker Eligibility and Assignment\n\n- Only workers meeting the mandatory eligibility requirements may be recommended for a job.\n- An assignment must not be confirmed if the worker is ineligible or unavailable under the applicable rules.\n- Conflicting assignments must be prevented where the schedules or service requirements make them incompatible.\n- System recommendations must not be treated as final assignments without the required manager confirmation.\n- Reassignment must follow the same eligibility requirements as the original assignment.\n- Assignment decisions and significant changes must be recorded.\n\n### 6.3 Fairness and Equal Opportunity\n\n- Fair opportunity must be an explicit consideration in job allocation.\n- Workers must be assessed using documented, relevant and consistently applied criteria.\n- Workload and previous allocations should be considered when defining an appropriate fairness mechanism.\n- Mandatory skill, safety, availability and service requirements must not be bypassed merely to equalize allocation counts.\n- The allocation process should avoid systematically favoring the same eligible workers without a justified operational reason.\n- Managers must be able to handle justified exceptions, with appropriate recording and oversight.\n- Allocation outcomes should be evaluated using defined indicators rather than relying solely on the stated intention of the rules.\n\nThe final fairness mechanism must balance equitable access with worker suitability, service quality, availability and customer requirements. Its formula and measurement criteria remain to be defined.\n\n### 6.4 Request and Job Status Management\n\n- Every request must have a unique identifier and a traceable status.\n- Requests must follow defined and validated status transitions.\n- Only authorized users may accept, reject, cancel, assign or close a request.\n- Assignment and completion information must remain associated with the relevant service request.\n- Completion must follow the approved recording or verification process.\n- Material changes must preserve sufficient history for accountability.\n\n### 6.5 Administrative Governance\n\n- Administrative permissions must reflect the approved central, state and cooperative operating model.\n- Important administrative changes must be attributable to the responsible user.\n- Changes to common policies and allocation rules must be controlled and documented.\n- Escalations must be directed to an authorized level of responsibility.\n- Reports must disclose only information appropriate to the recipient's role and scope.\n\n### 6.6 Data Protection and Operational Integrity\n\n- The platform must collect and expose only the information necessary for authorized operations.\n- Sensitive information must be protected against unauthorized access.\n- Request, assignment and completion records must remain consistent.\n- Financial records, if implemented, must be traceable and handled separately from assumptions about completed payments.\n- Data retention, correction, deletion and audit requirements must be defined according to applicable obligations.\n\n### 6.7 Business Policies Requiring Validation\n\nThe following decisions must be finalized before the corresponding requirements are treated as confirmed:\n\n- Identity and organizational verification procedures.\n- Worker acceptance or rejection of assignments.\n- Exact allocation and fairness formula.\n- Cancellation, rescheduling and reassignment rules.\n- Service pricing, payment handling and settlement responsibilities.\n- Institutional authorization and contract requirements.\n- Job completion verification and dispute-resolution processes.\n- Division of responsibilities between central and state administrators.\n- Data retention, reporting and privacy policies.\n- Applicable performance, availability and recovery targets.\n\n## Scope Management Note\n\nThis document defines the intended full-platform scope at a working level. It does not establish that every capability listed above is already approved, legally validated or feasible for immediate implementation.\n\nThe requirements documents will elaborate the relevant workflows, permissions, business rules and acceptance criteria. After the full platform has been documented, the team will evaluate the feature inventory and select a coherent, feasible Version 1 scope.\n\nThe approved MVP boundary supports individual customers through the complete service workflow, from discovery and request submission through cooperative review, fair allocation, assignment, execution, completion and payment-status recording. Institutional customers and institutional service requests are deferred from MVP delivery; their full-platform scope remains documented for a later release. Institutional tenders, procurement and formal contract management remain conditional pending stakeholder validation.\n\nFeatures excluded from Version 1 may remain part of the longer-term platform. Any feature deliberately excluded from the overall platform should have a documented rationale.\n\n## 7. Important Decisions Pending\n\n### Stakeholders and Roles\n|Item\t|Current status|\n|---|---\n|Central platform with state-level administration\t        |Working direction established\n|Society-level workforce and job management\t                |Established in the scope\n|Manager confirms system-recommended worker assignments\t    |Established\n|Household and basic institutional requests\t                |Included in the intended platform\n|Dedicated support or verification role\t                    |Needs validation\n|Exact permissions for each role\t                        |To be specified\n|Who operates the central platform\t                        |Unresolved\n|Whether federations require their own role and dashboard\t|Unresolved\n\n### Core Business Workflows\n| Decision | Current status |\n| --- | --- |\n| Manager confirms system-recommended worker assignment | Established |\n| Household service requests | Included |\n| Basic institutional requests | Included |\n| Worker onboarding and verification process | Unresolved |\n| Worker acceptance or rejection of an assignment | Unresolved |\n| Customer cancellation and rescheduling policy | Unresolved |\n| Completion verification responsibility | Unresolved |\n| Complaint and dispute escalation | Unresolved |\n| Institutional contract and payment workflow | Unresolved |\n| Exact central/state/cooperative authority boundaries | Unresolved |\n","srs":"# Cooperative GIG\n## Software Requirements Specification (SRS)\n\n**Version:** 1.0 Draft  \n**Status:** Working Baseline — Pending Review  \n**Project:** Cooperative Gig Services Platform for Household and Community Services  \n**Document purpose:** Define the intended full platform before selecting the features for Version 1.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Introduction\n\n### 1.1 Purpose\n\nCooperative GIG is a digital platform intended to help labour cooperative societies manage their workforce, coordinate service requests, distribute work opportunities fairly, negotiate service prices and maintain accountability between workers and customers.\n\nThis SRS defines the platform's intended functionality, users, workflows, business rules, security requirements and operational constraints. It will serve as the reference for feature prioritization, system architecture, database design, API development, testing and implementation planning.\n\nThis document describes the full-platform vision. It does not imply that all specified capabilities will be implemented in the first release.\n\n### 1.2 Problem statement\n\nLabour cooperative societies have skilled workers who can provide household, community and institutional services. However, customers need a structured way to discover these services, request work, agree on pricing and track service delivery.\n\nCooperatives also need effective tools to manage workers, assess job requirements, coordinate assignments, monitor service quality and resolve issues between workers and customers.\n\nA fixed-price model may not suit every service because the final cost can depend on the work's complexity, duration, materials and specific requirements. Similarly, assigning work without considering the distribution of opportunities may result in some eligible workers receiving more opportunities than others.\n\nCooperative GIG aims to address these problems through a cooperative-oriented platform that combines service coordination, worker ranking, negotiated pricing, payment records and administrative oversight.\n\n### 1.3 Objectives\n\n1. Enable customers to discover services and submit requests.\n2. Help cooperatives manage workers, customers and service operations.\n3. Develop an algorithm that ranks suitable workers and supports equitable job opportunities.\n4. Allow workers to accept or reject assignment offers.\n5. Facilitate price negotiation between workers and customers.\n6. Record agreed service scope, price and payment terms.\n7. Track jobs from request submission through completion.\n8. Support household, community and institutional service requests.\n9. Provide central-level monitoring, state-level administration and cooperative-level operational management.\n10. Maintain appropriate security, auditability and accountability.\n11. Provide a scalable foundation for additional financial, reporting and integration capabilities.\n\n### 1.4 Scope boundary\n\nThe full platform may include workforce management, service discovery, booking coordination, worker ranking, negotiated pricing, payment tracking, complaint management, administrative reporting and future integrations.\n\nThe MVP will be selected separately after the requirements have been reviewed and prioritized.\n\n### 1.5 Terminology\n\n- **Service request:** A customer's or institution's request for a service.\n- **Worker recommendation:** A worker suggested by the ranking algorithm.\n- **Assignment offer:** An offer sent to a worker to perform a particular job.\n- **Accepted offer:** An offer the worker agrees to consider or undertake, subject to the remaining required agreements.\n- **Negotiation:** The exchange of quotes and counteroffers between a worker and customer.\n- **Agreed service:** A request for which the applicable parties have agreed to the scope, price and required terms.\n- **Confirmed assignment:** An assignment that satisfies the platform's required acceptance and agreement conditions.\n- **Cooperative manager:** An authorized person responsible for a cooperative's operational management.\n- **Fair allocation:** A process designed to distribute suitable work opportunities equitably among eligible workers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Overall Platform Description\n\n### 2.1 Intended operating model\n\nCooperative GIG will use a centralized digital platform with administrative responsibilities distributed across organizational levels.\n\n**Central platform administration**\n- Monitor overall platform operations.\n- Access authorized platform-wide reports and aggregated indicators.\n- Manage explicitly authorized common settings and controls.\n- Maintain oversight without routinely taking over cooperative-level operations.\n\n**State administration**\n- Register and manage cooperatives within the authorized state scope.\n- Maintain cooperative records and relevant administrative information.\n- Monitor state-level operations and access permitted reports.\n\n**Cooperative management**\n- Manage workers, services and operational records.\n- Review incoming requests and coordinate service delivery.\n- Review worker rankings and send assignment offers.\n- Support price negotiation, monitor job progress and handle service issues.\n- Maintain appropriate relationships between workers and customers.\n\nA cooperative operating at a central or national level must retain its cooperative-management capabilities. Its administrative scope does not automatically replace its operational role.\n\n### 2.2 User classes\n\n| User | Primary responsibilities |\n|---|---|\n| Customer | Discover services, submit requests, negotiate price, track jobs and provide feedback. |\n| Institutional customer | Submit organizational requirements and coordinate service delivery. |\n| Worker | Maintain profile information, respond to assignment offers, negotiate service terms and perform jobs. |\n| Cooperative manager | Manage workforce and services, review requests, coordinate assignments and resolve operational issues. |\n| State administrator | Register and manage authorized cooperatives and oversee state-level operations. |\n| Platform administrator | Monitor overall operations and manage authorized platform-wide functions. |\n| Support or verification personnel | Perform assigned verification, support or complaint-handling duties if required. |\n\n### 2.3 Platform assumptions\n\n- The platform will support multiple cooperatives.\n- Each cooperative will have a defined organizational identity and operational scope.\n- Customers and workers will interact through authenticated accounts where required.\n- Workers must be able to accept or reject assignment offers.\n- Price negotiation will be supported for services that do not use a fixed price.\n- Worker ranking will be implemented through documented algorithmic rules.\n- The initial client direction is web-based, with Node.js preferred for the backend.\n- The precise ownership and operating organization of the central platform remain unresolved.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Functional Requirements\n\n### 3.1 Accounts and access management\n\n- **FR-AUTH-001:** The platform shall authenticate users before allowing access to protected functionality.\n- **FR-AUTH-002:** The platform shall support role-based permissions.\n- **FR-AUTH-003:** Authorization shall account for organizational scope, including the user's permitted state or cooperative.\n- **FR-AUTH-004:** Users shall be able to maintain permitted account and profile information.\n- **FR-AUTH-005:** The platform shall support appropriate account verification, recovery and status-management processes.\n- **FR-AUTH-006:** Unauthorized access to protected records or operations shall be rejected.\n- **FR-AUTH-007:** The platform shall distinguish user identity, role, organizational affiliation and assigned permissions.\n\n### 3.2 Service catalogue and discovery\n\n- **FR-SVC-001:** Customers shall be able to browse available service categories and descriptions.\n- **FR-SVC-002:** Customers shall be able to identify cooperatives offering relevant services.\n- **FR-SVC-003:** The platform shall maintain information about service requirements and applicable service conditions.\n- **FR-SVC-004:** Authorized cooperative personnel shall be able to maintain their service listings.\n- **FR-SVC-005:** The platform shall support relevant discovery criteria, such as location and service category, where applicable.\n- **FR-SVC-006:** Pricing information shall distinguish fixed prices, indicative prices and prices requiring negotiation.\n\n### 3.3 Customer service requests\n\n- **FR-REQ-001:** Customers shall be able to submit service requests with the required service details.\n- **FR-REQ-002:** Requests shall record relevant information, including location, preferred schedule and work description.\n- **FR-REQ-003:** Customers may provide an optional budget or expected price range.\n- **FR-REQ-004:** The platform shall validate required request information before accepting submission.\n- **FR-REQ-005:** Each submitted request shall receive a unique identifier.\n- **FR-REQ-006:** The platform shall make requests available to the appropriate cooperative for review.\n- **FR-REQ-007:** Authorized managers shall be able to accept a request for processing, reject it or request clarification.\n- **FR-REQ-008:** Customers shall be able to view the status of their requests.\n- **FR-REQ-009:** The platform shall support permitted cancellation and rescheduling requests.\n- **FR-REQ-010:** Customers shall be able to view relevant historical requests and outcomes.\n\n### 3.4 Worker profiles and lifecycle\n\n- **FR-WRK-001:** The platform shall maintain worker profiles containing relevant skills and service-related information.\n- **FR-WRK-002:** Workers shall be associated with the appropriate cooperative or cooperatives according to the approved membership model.\n- **FR-WRK-003:** Authorized personnel shall be able to verify worker information and manage eligibility status.\n- **FR-WRK-004:** The platform shall record worker availability information where provided.\n- **FR-WRK-005:** Workers shall be able to view their assignment offers and confirmed assignments.\n- **FR-WRK-006:** Workers shall be able to accept or reject assignment offers.\n- **FR-WRK-007:** The platform shall record the response and timestamp for each assignment offer.\n- **FR-WRK-008:** Workers shall be able to update job progress through permitted status transitions.\n- **FR-WRK-009:** Workers shall be able to report unavailability, delays or inability to complete a job.\n- **FR-WRK-010:** The platform shall retain relevant worker assignment and completion history.\n- **FR-WRK-011:** Workers or authorized personnel shall be able to maintain recorded worker availability according to the approved availability policy.\n\n### 3.5 Worker-ranking algorithm\n\n- **FR-RANK-001:** The platform shall implement an algorithm to rank workers for a service request.\n- **FR-RANK-002:** The algorithm shall evaluate workers against the request's relevant skill, service and other suitability requirements.\n- **FR-RANK-003:** The algorithm shall consider workload and previous job allocations to support equitable distribution of opportunities.\n- **FR-RANK-004:** The algorithm shall consider recorded availability as a relevant factor according to the approved ranking policy, but unavailable status shall not automatically prevent an assignment offer from being sent.\n- **FR-RANK-005:** The platform shall present ranked recommendations to an authorized cooperative manager.\n- **FR-RANK-006:** The platform shall allow an authorized manager to select a candidate from the recommended workers, subject to eligibility and governance rules.\n- **FR-RANK-007:** The platform shall record the selected worker and relevant assignment decision information.\n- **FR-RANK-008:** The platform shall retain sufficient allocation history to evaluate the distribution of opportunities.\n- **FR-RANK-009:** The platform shall support monitoring for persistent imbalances in job opportunities.\n- **FR-RANK-010:** The platform shall support the recording of justified manager overrides according to the approved policy.\n\nThe ranking formula, factor weights, tie-breaking rules and fairness metrics must be specified in a separate algorithm design. They are not yet finalized.\n\n### 3.6 Assignment offers and acceptance\n\n- **FR-ASG-001:** An authorized cooperative manager shall be able to send an assignment offer to a selected worker.\n- **FR-ASG-002:** An offer may be sent even if the worker's recorded availability indicates that they are unavailable.\n- **FR-ASG-003:** The worker shall be able to accept or reject the offer.\n- **FR-ASG-004:** The platform shall record the offer's pending, accepted, rejected or expired state as applicable.\n- **FR-ASG-005:** A rejected or expired offer shall not become a confirmed assignment.\n- **FR-ASG-006:** The platform shall support offering the job to another ranked candidate after rejection or expiry.\n- **FR-ASG-007:** The platform shall prevent incompatible confirmed assignments according to the approved scheduling rules.\n- **FR-ASG-008:** An accepted offer shall proceed to the required price and scope agreement process when negotiation is necessary.\n- **FR-ASG-009:** A confirmed assignment shall satisfy the applicable worker-acceptance, customer-agreement and cooperative-approval conditions.\n- **FR-ASG-010:** The platform shall retain a traceable history of offers, responses and assignment changes.\n\n### 3.7 Price negotiation\n\n- **FR-NEG-001:** The platform shall support negotiated pricing for services without a predefined fixed price.\n- **FR-NEG-002:** Workers shall be able to submit a quote for the proposed service.\n- **FR-NEG-003:** A quote may include the proposed amount, work scope, estimated duration, cost breakdown and payment terms where applicable.\n- **FR-NEG-004:** Customers shall be able to accept a quote, reject it, request clarification or submit a counteroffer.\n- **FR-NEG-005:** Workers shall be able to respond to counteroffers.\n- **FR-NEG-006:** The platform shall maintain a history of quotes, counteroffers and revisions.\n- **FR-NEG-007:** The platform shall distinguish proposed prices from the final agreed price.\n- **FR-NEG-008:** The platform shall record the final agreed amount, work scope, schedule and payment terms.\n- **FR-NEG-009:** The platform shall not treat the price as agreed until the required parties have accepted the same terms.\n- **FR-NEG-010:** The platform shall support negotiation expiry or timeout policies if adopted.\n- **FR-NEG-011:** If the parties cannot agree, the request shall follow the approved decline, closure or reassignment process.\n- **FR-NEG-012:** Changes to agreed work scope or price shall require the applicable approvals and a recorded revision.\n\n### 3.8 Payment management\n\n- **FR-PAY-001:** The platform shall maintain the agreed price and payment terms associated with a service.\n- **FR-PAY-002:** The platform shall support a configurable payment model appropriate to the service and cooperative policy.\n- **FR-PAY-003:** The platform shall record payment obligations and outstanding balances.\n- **FR-PAY-004:** The platform shall record payment status and relevant transaction information.\n- **FR-PAY-005:** The platform shall distinguish a declared cash payment from a digitally verified transaction.\n- **FR-PAY-006:** Digital payment integration may be supported through an approved payment provider.\n- **FR-PAY-007:** The platform shall support recording of refunds, adjustments or partial payments where applicable.\n- **FR-PAY-008:** The platform shall support authorized review of payment disputes.\n- **FR-PAY-009:** The platform shall maintain a traceable history of financial status changes.\n- **FR-PAY-010:** Financial information shall be accessible only to authorized users.\n- **FR-PAY-011:** Cooperative fees, commissions or revenue-sharing rules shall be configurable according to an approved policy rather than assuming one universal fee.\n- **FR-PAY-012:** The platform shall distinguish recording a payment from independently confirming that the money has been received.\n\nThe payment recipient, cooperative revenue model, fee policy and settlement responsibilities remain open decisions.\n\n### 3.9 Job execution and completion\n\n- **FR-JOB-001:** Workers shall be able to view the details of their confirmed jobs.\n- **FR-JOB-002:** Workers shall be able to update job status through permitted transitions.\n- **FR-JOB-003:** The platform shall record relevant progress and timestamps.\n- **FR-JOB-004:** Workers shall be able to report delays or inability to complete a job.\n- **FR-JOB-005:** The platform shall support completion information or evidence where required.\n- **FR-JOB-006:** The platform shall support the approved completion-verification process.\n- **FR-JOB-007:** Customers shall be able to view permitted job progress and completion information.\n- **FR-JOB-008:** The platform shall retain final job records and relevant assignment history.\n- **FR-JOB-009:** The platform shall support cancellation, reassignment and exception handling.\n- **FR-JOB-010:** The platform shall support customer feedback and service-related complaints where enabled.\n- **FR-JOB-011:** Customers and institutional customers shall be able to view permitted assignment information after an assignment is confirmed, subject to role and organizational access rules.\n\n### 3.10 Cooperative management\n\n- **FR-COOP-001:** Authorized managers shall be able to maintain cooperative profiles and service listings.\n- **FR-COOP-002:** Managers shall be able to manage worker records within their authorized scope.\n- **FR-COOP-003:** Managers shall be able to review and process incoming service requests.\n- **FR-COOP-004:** Managers shall be able to view ranked worker recommendations.\n- **FR-COOP-005:** Managers shall be able to send assignment offers and monitor responses.\n- **FR-COOP-006:** Managers shall be able to monitor active jobs and completion status.\n- **FR-COOP-007:** Managers shall be able to handle operational exceptions and reassignment.\n- **FR-COOP-008:** Managers shall be able to review relevant customer feedback and complaints.\n- **FR-COOP-009:** Managers shall be able to access relevant workforce and service-delivery reports.\n- **FR-COOP-010:** Cooperative records shall be protected from unauthorized access by other cooperatives.\n\n### 3.11 Central and state administration\n\n- **FR-ADM-001:** The platform shall support authorized platform-wide monitoring.\n- **FR-ADM-002:** Central administrators shall be able to view permitted aggregated platform indicators and reports.\n- **FR-ADM-003:** State administrators shall be able to register cooperatives within their authorized state scope.\n- **FR-ADM-004:** State administrators shall be able to maintain authorized cooperative records.\n- **FR-ADM-005:** State administrators shall be able to view relevant state-scoped operational reports.\n- **FR-ADM-006:** Administrative permissions shall be explicitly defined and enforced.\n- **FR-ADM-007:** Important administrative actions shall be recorded.\n- **FR-ADM-008:** Central monitoring shall not automatically grant unrestricted access to every cooperative's operational data.\n- **FR-ADM-009:** Cooperatives operating at a central level shall retain cooperative-management functionality.\n- **FR-ADM-010:** The platform shall support escalation of issues between the appropriate administrative levels.\n- **FR-ADM-011:** Changes to shared policies and allocation rules shall require authorized control and shall be traceable to the responsible actor, effective time and policy version.\n\n### 3.12 Institutional service management\n\n- **FR-INS-001:** Authorized institutional representatives shall be able to submit service requirements.\n- **FR-INS-002:** Institutional requests shall record relevant scope, location, schedule and workforce needs.\n- **FR-INS-003:** Cooperatives shall be able to review institutional requests and assess feasibility.\n- **FR-INS-004:** The platform shall record acceptance, rejection or requests for clarification.\n- **FR-INS-005:** Accepted institutional requests shall support workforce coordination and job tracking.\n- **FR-INS-006:** Institutions shall be able to view permitted service-delivery records.\n- **FR-INS-007:** Institutions shall be able to submit feedback or complaints.\n- **FR-INS-008:** The platform may support formal contracts, tenders and procurement workflows if validated.\n- **FR-INS-009:** Authorized institutional representatives shall be able to maintain permitted institutional organization and contact information.\n- **FR-INS-010:** Authorized institutional representatives shall be able to access relevant service-delivery reports within their permitted scope.\n- **FR-INS-011:** Institutional users may access permitted financial records when the corresponding payment and financial-reporting capabilities are implemented.\n\n### 3.13 Notifications and communication\n\n- **FR-NOT-001:** The platform shall notify relevant parties of request and booking status changes.\n- **FR-NOT-002:** Workers shall receive assignment-offer notifications.\n- **FR-NOT-003:** Customers and workers shall receive relevant quote and counteroffer updates.\n- **FR-NOT-004:** The platform shall communicate accepted, rejected or expired assignment offers.\n- **FR-NOT-005:** The platform shall communicate relevant cancellation, completion and payment-status changes.\n- **FR-NOT-006:** Notification delivery status shall be tracked where supported by the delivery channel.\n\n### 3.14 Feedback, complaints and disputes\n\n- **FR-DSP-001:** Customers shall be able to report service-related issues.\n- **FR-DSP-002:** The platform shall record complaint status and relevant history.\n- **FR-DSP-003:** Authorized personnel shall be able to review and resolve complaints.\n- **FR-DSP-004:** The platform shall support escalation of unresolved issues.\n- **FR-DSP-005:** Disputes relating to work scope, completion, price or payment shall be recorded separately from ordinary booking status.\n- **FR-DSP-006:** Resolution decisions shall be attributable to authorized personnel.\n\n### 3.15 Reporting and analytics\n\n- **FR-REP-001:** Cooperatives shall be able to review relevant service-request and completion information.\n- **FR-REP-002:** Authorized personnel shall be able to review worker workload and utilization.\n- **FR-REP-003:** The platform shall support analysis of job-allocation patterns.\n- **FR-REP-004:** State administrators shall be able to access permitted state-level reports.\n- **FR-REP-005:** Central administrators shall be able to access permitted platform-level reports.\n- **FR-REP-006:** Financial reporting may be supported if payment and settlement capabilities are adopted.\n- **FR-REP-007:** Reports shall respect role and organizational access boundaries.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Business Rules\n\n### 4.1 Request and assignment rules\n\n- **BR-001:** Every request must have a unique identifier.\n- **BR-002:** Submission does not mean the request has been accepted.\n- **BR-003:** Only an authorized manager can initiate an assignment offer on behalf of a cooperative.\n- **BR-004:** An assignment offer is not a confirmed assignment.\n- **BR-005:** A worker must respond to an assignment offer by accepting or rejecting it.\n- **BR-006:** Rejected or expired offers must not become confirmed assignments.\n- **BR-007:** The platform must prevent incompatible confirmed assignments under the approved scheduling rules.\n- **BR-008:** Confirmed assignments must satisfy the applicable acceptance and service-agreement requirements.\n\n### 4.2 Fair allocation rules\n\n- **BR-009:** Worker recommendations must follow documented ranking rules.\n- **BR-010:** Suitability requirements must be considered alongside fair opportunity.\n- **BR-011:** Availability information must not automatically block an offer under the currently intended workflow.\n- **BR-012:** Allocation history must be retained sufficiently to evaluate opportunity distribution.\n- **BR-013:** Manager overrides must follow the approved policy.\n- **BR-014:** Fairness must be evaluated using defined indicators rather than assuming that equal job counts always constitute fairness.\n- **BR-029:** Fair-allocation rules must not bypass mandatory suitability, safety or service-eligibility requirements merely to equalize opportunity measures.\n\n### 4.3 Negotiation and financial rules\n\n- **BR-015:** A proposed quote is not a final agreed price.\n- **BR-016:** The required parties must agree to the same terms before the service is confirmed under the negotiated-pricing workflow.\n- **BR-017:** Changes to agreed scope or price require the applicable approvals.\n- **BR-018:** Payment records must distinguish amounts due, payments declared, transactions confirmed and balances outstanding.\n- **BR-019:** A recorded cash payment must not be represented as independently verified unless the platform has an appropriate verification basis.\n- **BR-020:** Fees and revenue sharing must follow an approved cooperative or platform policy.\n- **BR-021:** Payment disputes must follow the approved review and resolution process.\n\n### 4.4 Governance and data rules\n\n- **BR-022:** Users may access only the functions and records authorized for their role and organizational scope.\n- **BR-023:** State administrators must operate within their authorized state scope.\n- **BR-024:** Cooperative managers must be restricted to their authorized cooperative records.\n- **BR-025:** Central monitoring privileges must not automatically imply unrestricted operational authority.\n- **BR-026:** Significant request, assignment, negotiation, financial and administrative changes must be traceable.\n- **BR-027:** Job statuses must follow permitted transitions.\n- **BR-028:** Data access and reporting must respect applicable privacy requirements.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Non-Functional Requirements\n\n### 5.1 Security\n\n- **NFR-SEC-001:** Protected functionality must require authentication.\n- **NFR-SEC-002:** Authorization must be enforced by backend services.\n- **NFR-SEC-003:** Sensitive information must be protected against unauthorized access.\n- **NFR-SEC-004:** Passwords, tokens, credentials and application secrets must be handled securely.\n- **NFR-SEC-005:** Inputs must be validated, and errors must not expose secrets or sensitive implementation details.\n- **NFR-SEC-006:** Security testing must cover critical workflows and access boundaries.\n- **NFR-SEC-007:** The platform shall support approved policies and controlled processes for data retention, correction and deletion, subject to legal, audit and dispute-preservation requirements.\n\n### 5.2 Data integrity and auditability\n\n- **NFR-DAT-001:** Request, assignment, negotiation and payment records must remain internally consistent.\n- **NFR-DAT-002:** Failed operations must not silently leave records in unintended states.\n- **NFR-DAT-003:** Critical changes must be traceable to the responsible user or system process.\n- **NFR-DAT-004:** The platform must preserve the history needed to investigate assignment and payment disputes.\n- **NFR-DAT-005:** Financial amounts must use appropriate precision and currency representation.\n\n### 5.3 Reliability and performance\n\n- **NFR-REL-001:** Duplicate submissions and conflicting assignments must be handled safely.\n- **NFR-REL-002:** Backup and recovery procedures must be documented.\n- **NFR-PER-001:** Common operations must meet agreed response-time targets under expected load.\n- **NFR-PER-002:** The system must support growth in users, cooperatives and service requests without requiring a complete redesign.\n- **NFR-PER-003:** Reporting and analytics must not unreasonably disrupt core booking operations.\n\nQuantitative performance, availability and recovery targets remain to be established.\n\n### 5.4 Usability and accessibility\n\n- **NFR-USE-001:** Interfaces must present clear status descriptions and understandable actions.\n- **NFR-USE-002:** Forms must provide clear validation feedback.\n- **NFR-USE-003:** Core workflows must be usable on supported device sizes.\n- **NFR-USE-004:** Language and accessibility requirements must be determined for the intended user population.\n- **NFR-USE-005:** Customers and workers must be able to understand relevant booking, negotiation and assignment outcomes.\n\n### 5.5 Maintainability and testing\n\n- **NFR-MNT-001:** The codebase must have clear module boundaries.\n- **NFR-MNT-002:** Ranking and pricing rules must be testable independently of the user interface.\n- **NFR-MNT-003:** Automated tests must cover critical workflows, authorization and business rules.\n- **NFR-MNT-004:** Changes must be reviewed and tested before merging into the primary branch.\n- **NFR-MNT-005:** API and data-model changes must be documented.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Proposed Status Models\n\nThese models establish the distinctions the platform must preserve. Exact transition permissions and timeout policies will be finalized during detailed design.\n\n### 6.1 Service request\n\nProposed states:\n\n`Submitted → Under Review → Accepted for Processing / Rejected`\n\nAn accepted request may proceed to worker ranking and assignment offers.\n\n### 6.2 Assignment offer\n\nProposed states:\n\n`Pending Response → Accepted / Rejected / Expired / Withdrawn`\n\nAn accepted offer proceeds to price and scope agreement where negotiation is required.\n\n### 6.3 Negotiation\n\nProposed states:\n\n`Awaiting Worker Quote → Quote Submitted → Counteroffer Pending → Agreed / Declined / Expired`\n\nThe platform must support multiple quote revisions without losing previous offers.\n\n### 6.4 Confirmed job\n\nProposed states:\n\n`Confirmed → In Progress → Completed`\n\nAlternative outcomes may include `Cancelled`, `Unable to Complete` or `Disputed`. The exact state machine will specify which roles can perform each transition.\n\n### 6.5 Payment\n\nProposed states:\n\n`Not Due → Due → Partially Paid / Payment Reported / Payment Processing → Paid / Failed / Disputed / Refunded`\n\nThe final model must distinguish declared payment, payment-provider confirmation and actual settlement. These states are not interchangeable.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Acceptance Criteria\n\nThe requirements will be considered verifiable when tests can establish the following outcomes.\n\n| Area | Acceptance condition |\n|---|---|\n| Authentication | Unauthorized users cannot access protected operations. |\n| Organizational boundaries | Users cannot access records outside their permitted scope. |\n| Service requests | Valid requests receive unique references and invalid requests produce clear errors. |\n| Worker ranking | The algorithm follows the documented criteria and produces reproducible results for equivalent inputs. |\n| Fair allocation | Allocation history supports evaluation against the defined fairness indicators. |\n| Availability | A worker marked unavailable can still receive an offer under the specified workflow. |\n| Assignment response | Rejected or expired offers do not become confirmed assignments. |\n| Negotiation | Quote and counteroffer history is retained, and the agreed price is recorded only after the required agreement. |\n| Scope changes | A price or scope change requires the specified approvals and creates a traceable revision. |\n| Payment tracking | Declared, processing, confirmed, outstanding and disputed amounts are distinguishable. |\n| Job execution | Only permitted status transitions are accepted and recorded. |\n| Administration | Central, state and cooperative permissions are enforced. |\n| Auditability | Significant decisions and changes can be traced. |\n| Reliability | Critical failures do not create inconsistent requests, assignments or financial records. |\n\nDetailed test cases will be produced after the status transitions, allocation formula, payment policies and permissions are approved.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Assumptions, Risks and Open Decisions\n\n### 8.1 Established direction\n\n- Cooperative management is the operational centre of the platform.\n- Central administration focuses on overall monitoring and authorized platform-wide controls.\n- State administrators register and manage cooperatives within their authorized scope.\n- Worker recommendations are generated by a ranking algorithm.\n- Workers must accept or reject assignment offers.\n- Offers may be sent regardless of recorded availability.\n- Worker and customer negotiate price where a fixed price is not appropriate.\n- Payment tracking must accommodate more than one payment method.\n- A universal fixed fee is not assumed.\n\n### 8.2 Decisions still requiring definition\n\n1. **Ranking algorithm:** Factor weights, fairness measurements, tie-breaking and treatment of unavailable workers.\n2. **Offer timeout:** How long a worker has to respond and whether reminders are sent.\n3. **Negotiation timeout:** How long quotes remain valid and what happens when negotiation fails.\n4. **Worker selection:** Whether managers can select any eligible candidate or must follow ranking order unless an override is justified.\n5. **Confirmation:** Whether cooperative approval is required after price agreement and worker acceptance.\n6. **Pricing policy:** Whether cooperatives may establish minimum or maximum prices, review quotes or intervene only in exceptions.\n7. **Payment recipient:** Whether customers pay workers directly, pay cooperatives or use another approved arrangement.\n8. **Fees:** Whether cooperatives or the platform charge commissions, membership fees or service fees.\n9. **Cash payments:** What evidence or confirmation is required before recording payment as settled.\n10. **Digital payments:** Which provider and transaction model, if any, will be used.\n11. **Completion verification:** Who confirms completion and how disputes are handled.\n12. **Institutional contracts:** Whether formal contracts, tenders and procurement are part of the intended platform.\n13. **Governance:** Exact central and state permissions, including suspension, verification and dispute escalation.\n14. **Operating organization:** Who legally owns or operates the central platform.\n15. **Non-functional targets:** Expected load, response time, availability, backup and recovery requirements.\n16. **Shared-policy governance:** Which authorities approve shared-policy changes, how policy versions become effective and how historical versions are retained.\n17. **Data lifecycle:** Retention periods, correction procedures, deletion exceptions and preservation requirements for legal, audit or dispute purposes.\n\n### 8.3 Principal risks\n\n| Risk | Mitigation direction |\n|---|---|\n| Unfair ranking outcomes | Document criteria, retain allocation history and evaluate results. |\n| Offers sent to unavailable workers | Make offer status explicit, require worker response and prevent incompatible confirmed assignments. |\n| Failed price negotiations | Support counteroffers, expiry and reassignment. |\n| Price or scope disputes | Preserve quote history and require recorded agreement for changes. |\n| Unverified payments | Distinguish reported payments from independently confirmed transactions. |\n| Unclear cooperative authority | Define role and organization permissions before implementation. |\n| Excessive first-release scope | Select the MVP from this specification using feasibility and priority criteria. |\n| Deferred institutional workflows | Keep institutional requirements intact for a later release and validate institutional permissions and delivery policies before implementation. |\n| Inadequate requirements validation | Review unresolved policies before finalizing affected functionality. |\n\n---\n\n## 9. MVP Selection Framework\n\nThe MVP will be selected from the requirements in this SRS after review. The following are candidate modules, not finalized release commitments:\n\n1. Authentication and role-based access.\n2. Service catalogue and customer requests.\n3. Worker profiles and cooperative management.\n4. Worker-ranking algorithm and allocation history.\n5. Assignment offers and worker acceptance or rejection.\n6. Negotiated quotes and customer counteroffers.\n7. Recording of agreed price and payment terms.\n8. Job tracking and completion records.\n9. Basic central and state administration.\n10. Institutional services as a later-release capability; institutional requests are excluded from the approved MVP boundary.\n11. Notifications, feedback and complaints.\n12. Digital payment integration, advanced financial settlement and analytics.\n\nEach candidate will be assessed for importance, implementation effort, dependencies, risk, testability and demonstration value.\n\nThe MVP should demonstrate a coherent end-to-end service workflow. Features deferred from Version 1 remain part of the full-platform vision unless explicitly removed through a documented scope decision.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Requirements Governance\n\n1. Every functional requirement must have a unique identifier.\n2. Requirements must be classified as established, proposed or pending validation.\n3. Related business rules, dependencies and acceptance criteria must be traceable.\n4. Changes to the approved requirements baseline must be documented.\n5. The full-platform specification must remain distinct from the Version 1 scope.\n6. Technical design must follow the approved requirements rather than introduce undocumented business assumptions.\n7. Requirements are ready for implementation when the behavior, permissions, relevant exceptions and acceptance criteria are sufficiently clear.\n\n## 11. Definition of SRS Readiness\n\nThis SRS becomes ready for approval when:\n\n- The roles and operating model have been reviewed.\n- The customer, worker and cooperative workflows are agreed.\n- Ranking, offer acceptance and negotiated pricing are sufficiently specified.\n- Payment and financial responsibilities have been defined to the level required by the selected scope.\n- Organizational permissions and administrative boundaries are documented.\n- Non-functional requirements have measurable targets where practical.\n- Open decisions are either resolved or explicitly accepted as deferred.\n- The requirements are ready to be prioritized into a separate Version 1 backlog.\n","proposed":"# Cooperative GIG — Proposed MVP Scope\n\n**Status:** Proposed MVP scope for review  \n**Source documents:** `project-scope.md`, `SRS.md`, `feature-inventory.md`  \n**MVP audience:** Individual customers, workers and cooperative operations  \n**Client direction:** Web-first; Node.js backend remains a proposed technical direction\n\nThis document selects an MVP from the full-platform inventory. Existing P0/P1/P2 values remain full-platform priorities; the classifications below are MVP decisions and do not change those priorities or the full-platform requirements.\n\nInstitutional customers and institutional service requests are outside this MVP. `INS-01`–`INS-03` remain Later full-platform capabilities. `INS-04` remains Conditional and outside MVP pending stakeholder validation.\n\n## 1. Core MVP feature matrix\n\n| Feature ID | Feature | MVP classification | MVP implementation scope | SRS references | Dependencies | Acceptance criteria |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| ID-01 | User registration and authentication | Must | Authenticate individual customers, workers and authorized cooperative users. | `FR-AUTH-001, FR-AUTH-005` | User model, authentication service | Valid users authenticate; invalid credentials are rejected. |\n| ID-02 | Role and permission management | Must | Implement customer, worker and cooperative-manager permissions; retain extensible administrative roles. | `FR-AUTH-002, FR-AUTH-006–007` | ID-01, organizational model | A user cannot perform an action outside the assigned role. |\n| ID-03 | Organization-scoped access | Must | Enforce cooperative-level isolation for every MVP request, worker, assignment and payment record. | `FR-AUTH-003` | ID-02, cooperative records | A user cannot retrieve another cooperative’s restricted records. |\n| ID-04 | Account recovery and status management | Should | Provide recovery and inactive/suspended account controls; recovery-channel details remain policy-dependent. | `FR-AUTH-005` | ID-01, notification mechanism | A recovery request follows the approved process, and a prohibited action by an inactive/suspended account is rejected. |\n| ID-05 | Profile management | Must | Support permitted customer, worker and cooperative-user profile fields. | `FR-AUTH-004` | ID-01, role profiles | Permitted profile changes succeed; invalid or unauthorized changes fail. |\n| SVC-01 | Service categories and catalogue | Must | Provide active household and community services with descriptions and requirements. | `FR-SVC-001, 003` | Service data model | An individual customer can browse active services and requirements. |\n| SVC-02 | Cooperative service listings | Must | Show which cooperatives offer each service; allow authorized managers to maintain listings. | `FR-SVC-002, 004` | Cooperative records, SVC-01 | A customer can identify an offering cooperative. |\n| SVC-03 | Service search and filtering | Should | Provide practical location/category filtering where data is reliable. | `FR-SVC-005` | SVC-01, SVC-02 | A selected filter returns matching services. |\n| SVC-04 | Pricing-type configuration | Must | Distinguish fixed, indicative and negotiable service pricing. | `FR-SVC-006` | SVC-01, pricing policy | The displayed pricing type is unambiguous. |\n| REQ-01 | Household/community service requests | Must | Support individual-customer requests with service, location, schedule and description. | `FR-REQ-001–005` | ID-01, SVC-01, SVC-02 | A valid request receives a unique reference; invalid input is rejected. |\n| REQ-02 | Request review and clarification | Must | Allow a cooperative manager to accept, reject or request clarification. | `FR-REQ-006–007` | REQ-01, cooperative permissions | Each manager decision is recorded with status and actor. |\n| REQ-03 | Booking status and history | Must | Expose current and historical individual-customer request outcomes. | `FR-REQ-008, 010` | REQ-01, status model | A customer can view current status and prior outcomes. |\n| REQ-04 | Cancellation and rescheduling | Should | Support policy-approved requests and recorded outcomes; exact policy remains open. | `FR-REQ-009` | REQ-01, status model | An unauthorized cancellation is rejected; an allowed action is traceable. |\n| REQ-05 | Customer budget input | Must | Capture an optional budget without forcing a fixed price. | `FR-REQ-003` | REQ-01, pricing model | Budget input does not make a negotiable service fixed-price. |\n| WRK-01 | Worker registration and cooperative association | Must | Onboard and associate workers with the authorized cooperative. | `FR-WRK-001–003` | ID-01, cooperative model | An approved worker is linked to the correct cooperative. |\n| WRK-02 | Skills and service eligibility | Must | Maintain skills, eligibility and mandatory service/safety information. | `FR-WRK-001, 003` | WRK-01, service catalogue | Only authorized users can change eligibility. |\n| WRK-03 | Availability management | Must | Maintain availability as a ranking/scheduling input; it is not an automatic offer exclusion. | `FR-WRK-004, FR-WRK-011, FR-RANK-004` | WRK-01, scheduling model | An unavailable worker may receive an offer under the approved workflow. |\n| WRK-04 | Worker work history and workload | Must | Retain assignment and workload data needed for fair allocation. | `FR-WRK-010, FR-RANK-003, 008` | Assignment records | Authorized users can retrieve relevant history. |\n| WRK-05 | Worker status and eligibility lifecycle | Must | Apply approved inactive, suspended and eligibility states. | `FR-WRK-003, FR-RANK-002` | WRK-01, WRK-02 | Ineligible workers are excluded where rules require it. |\n| RANK-01 | Eligibility filtering | Must | Exclude workers failing mandatory suitability, safety or service-eligibility requirements. | `FR-RANK-001, 002`, `BR-029` | WRK-02, WRK-03, REQ-01 | Mandatory failures are excluded and recorded. |\n| RANK-02 | Worker ranking algorithm | Must | Use deterministic, documented ranking with suitability, workload, previous allocations and availability factors. | `FR-RANK-001–004` | RANK-01, WRK-04, approved ranking policy | Equivalent inputs and policy versions produce reproducible rankings. |\n| RANK-03 | Manager recommendation interface | Must | Let managers review ranked candidates before sending offers. | `FR-RANK-005–006` | RANK-02, cooperative dashboard | A manager can review eligible ranked candidates. |\n| RANK-04 | Allocation history and decision records | Must | Record recommendations, selected worker, rationale and policy version. | `FR-RANK-007–008` | RANK-02, assignment records | Allocation decisions are traceable. |\n| RANK-05 | Fairness monitoring | Must | Provide the approved indicators for reviewing opportunity distribution. | `FR-RANK-009–010` | RANK-04, reporting | Authorized users can inspect defined fairness indicators. |\n| RANK-06 | Manager override and justification | Must | Permit only policy-approved overrides with justification and audit history. | `FR-RANK-010` | RANK-03, audit logging | An override without required justification is rejected. |\n| ASG-01 | Assignment offer creation | Must | Managers send offers to selected workers, including unavailable workers where permitted. | `FR-ASG-001–002` | RANK-03, cooperative permissions | An authorized manager can send an offer. |\n| ASG-02 | Accept/reject offer | Must | Workers accept or reject offers; responses and timestamps are retained. | `FR-WRK-006`, `FR-ASG-003–005` | ASG-01, worker interface | Accepted and rejected offers cannot be confused with confirmed assignments. |\n| ASG-03 | Offer expiry and withdrawal | Must | Implement the offer expiry/withdrawal state required for recovery and ranked-candidate reassignment; timeout duration remains an open policy decision. | `FR-ASG-004–006` | ASG-01, timeout policy, notifications | An expired or withdrawn offer cannot become confirmed, and its terminal state can trigger the approved reassignment path. |\n| ASG-04 | Ranked-candidate reassignment | Must | Offer another eligible ranked candidate after rejection/expiry and prevent conflicts. | `FR-ASG-006–007`, `FR-WRK-009` | RANK-02, ASG-02, scheduling rules | Reassignment follows eligibility and conflict rules. |\n| ASG-05 | Assignment confirmation | Must | Confirm only after worker response, required customer agreement, cooperative approval and conflict checks. | `FR-ASG-008–010` | ASG-02, NEG-04 where required | A recommendation or offer alone never creates a confirmed assignment. |\n| NEG-01 | Worker quote submission | Must | Support quotes for services without predefined fixed prices. | `FR-NEG-001–003` | ASG-02, SVC-04, pricing model | A quote records amount, scope, schedule and terms. |\n| NEG-02 | Customer acceptance and counteroffer | Must | Support customer accept/reject/counteroffer and worker response. | `FR-NEG-004–005` | NEG-01, customer interface | Counteroffers and responses are recorded. |\n| NEG-03 | Quote version history | Must | Preserve every quote and counteroffer; distinguish proposed from agreed price. | `FR-NEG-006–007` | NEG-01, NEG-02 | Prior versions remain retrievable. |\n| NEG-04 | Final agreement record | Must | Record agreed scope, schedule, price and payment terms before confirmation. | `FR-NEG-008–009` | NEG-01, NEG-02, agreement model | The agreement is created only after required parties accept the same terms. |\n| NEG-05 | Negotiation timeout and failure handling | Should | Support approved timeout, closure or reassignment behavior. | `FR-NEG-010–011` | NEG-01, notifications, timeout policy | Failed negotiation follows a defined path. |\n| NEG-06 | Scope and price change management | Should | Record approved post-agreement changes and preserve prior versions. | `FR-NEG-012` | NEG-04, audit logging | An unapproved scope/price change is rejected. |\n| PAY-01 | Payment terms and obligations | Must | Record agreed terms, amounts due and balances for individual-customer jobs. | `FR-PAY-001–003` | NEG-04, payment policy | Agreed payment obligations are retrievable. |\n| PAY-02 | Payment records and status tracking | Must | Record declared, processing, confirmed, outstanding and disputed states without gateway claims. | `FR-PAY-004–005, 012` | PAY-01, financial model | Statuses remain distinguishable. |\n| PAY-03 | Cash payment declarations | Must | Record cash declarations without representing them as independently verified. | `FR-PAY-005, 012` | PAY-02, confirmation policy | A cash declaration does not become verified without evidence. |\n| PAY-05 | Refunds, partial payments and adjustments | Should | Record approved adjustments and partial payments. | `FR-PAY-007` | PAY-02, financial policy | Balances update with traceable entries. |\n| PAY-06 | Financial disputes and reconciliation | Should | Track individual-customer payment disputes and resolutions. | `FR-PAY-008–009` | PAY-02, complaint workflow | A dispute has an attributable resolution history. |\n| PAY-07 | Cooperative fees and settlement rules | Conditional | Do not calculate fees or settlement until an approved cooperative/platform policy exists. | `FR-PAY-010–011` | Payment recipient and fee policy | No fee or revenue-sharing amount is produced without an approved policy. |\n| COOP-01 | Cooperative profile and service management | Must | Maintain cooperative profile and service listings within scope. | `FR-COOP-001–002` | ID-03, SVC-01 | Managers cannot edit another cooperative’s records. |\n| COOP-02 | Request and workforce operations dashboard | Must | Provide the manager view for requests, recommendations, offers and active jobs. | `FR-COOP-003–006` | REQ-02, WRK-01, RANK-03, ASG-01 | A manager can operate the complete individual-customer workflow. |\n| COOP-03 | Operational exception handling | Must | Support basic reassignment and failed-assignment handling; complaints and broader service issues remain reduced-scope extensions. | `FR-COOP-007–008` | ASG-04, JOB-03, JOB-06 | An authorized manager can record a failed assignment and initiate an eligible reassignment; broader complaint handling follows approved policy where enabled. |\n| COOP-04 | Cooperative reporting | Should | Provide basic request, assignment, completion and workforce summaries. | `FR-COOP-009` | Request, worker, assignment and job records | Reports are limited to the cooperative scope. |\n| JOB-01 | Worker job dashboard | Must | Show confirmed individual-customer jobs and service details. | `FR-JOB-001` | ASG-05, worker permissions | Workers can view confirmed jobs. |\n| JOB-02 | Job status updates | Must | Support permitted progress transitions and timestamps. | `FR-JOB-002–003` | JOB-01, status model | Invalid transitions are rejected. |\n| JOB-03 | Delays and inability to complete | Must | Let workers report inability or delay so the cooperative can recover through reassignment; broader exception workflows remain policy-dependent. | `FR-JOB-004, 009` | JOB-01, notification workflow | A failed-assignment report is recorded, visible to the cooperative and eligible for the approved reassignment path. |\n| JOB-04 | Completion evidence and verification | Must | Record and verify individual-customer completion; expose permitted assignment information. | `FR-JOB-005–008, FR-JOB-011` | JOB-02, completion policy | Completion follows the approved verification process. |\n| JOB-05 | Ratings and feedback | Later | Defer ratings and feedback until after the core completion workflow. | `FR-JOB-010` | JOB-04, customer interface | No rating is required for MVP completion; later submissions can remain linked to completed services. |\n| JOB-06 | Complaints and service disputes | Should | Record and resolve individual-customer issues separately from booking status. | `FR-JOB-010`, `FR-DSP-001–006` | JOB-04, complaint policy | Issues are attributable, escalatable and closable. |\n\n## 2. Minimal supporting capabilities\n\n| Feature ID | Feature | MVP classification | MVP implementation scope | SRS references | Dependencies | Acceptance criteria |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| ADM-03 | Administrative audit and escalation | Must | Implement minimum administrative audit and escalation needed for cooperative operations. | `FR-ADM-006–007, 010` | Role model, audit logging | Administrative actions identify actor, time and outcome. |\n| ADM-01 | Central platform monitoring | Should | Provide limited authorized oversight/aggregates only; broad platform reporting is deferred. | `FR-ADM-001–002, 008` | Audit records, reporting, scope permissions | Central access cannot bypass cooperative isolation. |\n| ADM-02 | State cooperative registration and management | Later | Preserve the multi-tenant model but defer broad state workflows from the pilot MVP. | `FR-ADM-003–005` | ID-03, organization model | Later implementation remains scoped to authorized states. |\n| ADM-04 | Shared policy management | Conditional | Requires approved policy authority and versioning before implementation. | `FR-ADM-009, FR-ADM-011` | Governance approval model | No shared policy change becomes effective without approved control. |\n| NOT-01 | Booking and job notifications | Must | Notify individual customers, workers and managers of core status changes. | `FR-NOT-001, 005` | Status-change events, notification service | Core request, assignment, completion and payment updates are delivered. |\n| NOT-02 | Assignment offer notifications | Must | Notify workers of offers and responses. | `FR-NOT-002, 004` | ASG-01, ASG-02 | Offer and response outcomes are accurately reflected. |\n| NOT-03 | Negotiation notifications | Should | Notify customers/workers of quotes and counteroffers. | `FR-NOT-003` | NEG-01, NEG-02 | Relevant parties receive negotiation updates. |\n| NOT-04 | Payment and complaint notifications | Should | Notify individual-customer parties of permitted payment and complaint changes. | `FR-NOT-005–006` | PAY-02, JOB-06 | Notification delivery status is retained where supported. |\n| REP-01 | Service operations reporting | Should | Provide basic individual-customer request and completion summaries. | `FR-REP-001` | Request, assignment and job records | Authorized users can review request volumes and outcomes. |\n| REP-02 | Workforce utilization reporting | Should | Provide basic recorded workload summaries. | `FR-REP-002` | WRK-04, assignment history | Reports match recorded workload data. |\n| REP-03 | Fair allocation analytics | Must | Provide the approved fairness indicators required to review MVP allocation. | `FR-REP-003` | RANK-04, RANK-05 | Authorized users can inspect allocation indicators. |\n| REP-04 | State and platform reporting | Later | Defer broad state/platform reports while retaining access-boundary design. | `FR-REP-004–005` | ADM-01, ADM-02, data-access policies | No deferred report is exposed as an MVP capability. |\n| REP-05 | Financial reporting | Conditional | Defer until payment and settlement policies are approved. | `FR-REP-006–007` | PAY-01–PAY-07 | Financial reports are not enabled without approved policy and permissions. |\n| PLT-01 | Backend authorization enforcement | Must | Enforce role and cooperative boundaries on every API. | `NFR-SEC-001–003` | ID-02, ID-03 | Direct API calls cannot bypass restrictions. |\n| PLT-02 | Audit trail | Must | Audit material allocation, assignment, administrative, negotiation and payment events. | `FR-RANK-007`, `FR-ADM-007`, `NFR-DAT-003–004` | Identity model, domain events | Material decisions retain actor, time and outcome. |\n| PLT-03 | Data validation and integrity | Must | Validate domain inputs and prevent unintended partial states. | `NFR-SEC-005`, `NFR-DAT-001–002` | API/domain validation | Invalid operations do not create inconsistent records. |\n| PLT-04 | Duplicate and concurrency protection | Must | Protect requests, offers, confirmations and payment records from duplicates/conflicts. | `NFR-REL-001` | Domain model, transactions | Concurrent assignment attempts are handled safely. |\n| PLT-05 | Backup and recovery | Must | Establish and verify basic backup/restore for the MVP deployment. | `NFR-REL-002` | Database, deployment infrastructure | A documented restore procedure succeeds in a test. |\n| PLT-06 | Automated testing and CI | Must | Test authorization, allocation, state transitions and critical workflows automatically. | `NFR-SEC-006`, `NFR-MNT-002–004` | Repository and test framework | Automated checks run and cover critical business rules. |\n| PLT-07 | API and architecture documentation | Must | Document the MVP interfaces and material data-model decisions. | `NFR-MNT-001, 005` | Architecture/API design | Core interfaces and changes are documented. |\n| PLT-08 | Performance and scaling controls | Should | Test agreed pilot targets; quantitative targets remain an open decision. | `NFR-PER-001–003` | Architecture, load assumptions | Performance tests evaluate approved targets. |\n| PLT-09 | Accessibility and responsive interface | Must | Provide responsive web workflows and a documented baseline accessibility check. | `NFR-USE-001–005` | Frontend design system | Core workflows work on supported screen sizes. |\n| PLT-10 | Privacy and data lifecycle controls | Must | Apply approved access, retention, correction and deletion controls. | `NFR-SEC-006–007` | Data classification, retention policy | Lifecycle actions follow approved policies. |\n\n## 3. Deferred and conditional scope\n\n| Feature ID | Feature | MVP classification | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| INS-01 | Institutional account and representative authorization | Later | Institutional customers are outside MVP; retain for the full platform. |\n| INS-02 | Institutional requirement submission | Later | Institutional requests are outside MVP. |\n| INS-03 | Institutional delivery tracking | Later | Institutional tracking, reports and conditional financial visibility are outside MVP. |\n| INS-04 | Contract, tender and procurement management | Conditional | Requires stakeholder validation; remains outside MVP. |\n| PAY-04 | Digital payment integration | Later | Gateway processing is excluded from MVP. |\n| JOB-05 | Ratings and feedback | Later | Valuable service-quality capability, but not required to complete the core workflow. |\n| PAY-07 | Cooperative fees and settlement rules | Conditional | Requires an approved fee, revenue-sharing and settlement policy; no calculation is enabled in MVP by default. |\n| FUT-01 | Advanced demand forecasting | Later | Requires historical data and validated need. |\n| FUT-02 | Advanced recommendation optimization | Later | Transparent baseline ranking is sufficient for MVP. |\n| FUT-03 | External welfare, insurance or support integrations | Conditional | Requires partners, legal basis and security review. |\n| FUT-04 | Dedicated Android application | Later | The initial release is web-first. |\n| FUT-05 | Advanced analytics and dashboards | Later | Defer until metrics and data volume justify it. |\n\n## 4. End-to-end MVP workflow\n\n1. An individual customer discovers an available service.\n2. The customer submits a household or community request.\n3. The cooperative accepts, rejects or requests clarification.\n4. The system filters and ranks suitable workers using transparent allocation rules.\n5. An authorized manager reviews candidates and sends an assignment offer.\n6. The worker accepts or rejects the offer.\n7. A rejected or expired offer may proceed to another eligible ranked candidate.\n8. The customer and worker negotiate terms when the service is not fixed-price.\n9. Required parties agree to the same scope, schedule, price and payment terms.\n10. The assignment is confirmed only after authorization and scheduling/conflict checks.\n11. The worker performs the job and updates permitted status values.\n12. Completion evidence is recorded and verified under the approved process.\n13. Payment terms, payment declarations, verification status and outstanding balances are maintained without processing gateway transactions.\n\nAvailability does not automatically prevent an offer. Confirmed assignments must obey approved conflict rules. Fair allocation cannot bypass mandatory eligibility or safety requirements. Payment records do not imply gateway processing or independently verified settlement.\n\n## 5. MVP completion criteria\n\nThe MVP is complete when:\n\n- An individual customer can discover, submit and track a request.\n- A cooperative manager can review requests and operate the allocation workflow.\n- Ranked recommendations are reproducible under a documented policy version.\n- Worker offers support acceptance and rejection, and offers remain distinct from confirmed assignments.\n- Negotiable terms are recorded consistently before confirmation.\n- Confirmed jobs can be tracked through completion and verification.\n- Payment terms, payment declarations, verification status and balances are maintained without gateway processing or an implied settlement confirmation.\n- Unauthorized cross-cooperative access is rejected and tested.\n- Material allocation, assignment, administrative, negotiation and payment actions are auditable.\n- The web application is responsive, deployable, automatically tested and covered by a verified backup/restore procedure.\n\nCriteria involving fairness indicators, conflict rules, completion verification, payment confirmation, retention and performance targets remain dependent on the unresolved decisions listed below.\n\n## 6. Implementation dependencies and risks\n\n- Role and cooperative-scope permissions must be agreed before authorization and data models are finalized.\n- Ranking weights, fairness indicators, tie-breaking and manager overrides must be approved before implementing `RANK-02`–`RANK-06`.\n- Availability meaning and scheduling conflicts must be defined before confirmation and reassignment logic is finalized.\n- Offer expiry, confirmation sequencing and negotiation timeouts affect state machines and notification APIs.\n- Completion verification and dispute authority affect job closure and payment status.\n- Rejected, expired or failed assignments require a defined reassignment and exception path; `ASG-03`, `ASG-04`, `JOB-03` and `COOP-03` provide the MVP recovery capability, while timeout and exception policies remain open.\n- Payment recipient, cash evidence and settlement semantics remain unresolved; no gateway behavior is assumed.\n- Retention, correction, deletion and dispute-preservation policies affect audit and data lifecycle design.\n- Pilot performance, availability, backup and recovery targets remain open.\n- Institutional features are intentionally deferred; shared components must not require institutional onboarding, while `INS-01`–`INS-03` and `INS-04` remain preserved in the full platform.\n\n## 7. Traceability check\n\nAll feature IDs and SRS references used in this document were checked against the current `feature-inventory.md` and `SRS.md`. No new requirement or feature IDs are introduced. Existing full-platform priorities remain unchanged. The institutional requirements and features remain in their source documents and are classified here as Later or Conditional only for MVP planning.\n"},"team":[["Pradum Kumar","Cloud and Android Development"],["Alok Kumar","Full-Stack Development and DevOps"],["Gurbaksh Kaur","Full-Stack Development and DevOps"],["Sandeep Kaur","Cybersecurity"],["Mridulika","Cloud and DevOps"],["Pratyush Raj","Cloud and Game Development"]]};
